hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","(1) Chapter on the obligation of wudu. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: O you who believe, when you stand for prayer - the verse. Evidence that this applies to some of those who stand and not others: Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, (ح), and Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, both from Sufyan, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform wudu for every prayer, then on the day of the Conquest he performed wudu and wiped over his leather socks and prayed all the prayers with one wudu. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, you have done something you never used to do. He said: I did it deliberately, O Umar. This wording is Ishaq's, and Ibn Hashim did not mention: and wiped over his leather socks."
"2","(2) Chapter on wudu from wind. Muhammad ibn Yahya and Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us, they said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no wudu except from a sound or a wind."
"3","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, and from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you finds something in prayer, let him not leave until he finds a smell or hears a sound."
"4","(3) Chapter on wudu from stool, urine and sleep. Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Asim, from Zirr, he said: I came to Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to order us, when we were on a journey, not to remove our leather socks for three days and their nights except from janabah, and not to remove them for stool, nor urine, nor sleep."
"5","(4) Chapter on wudu from madhy. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas informed us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man who comes close to his wife and emits madhy, and he said: If one of you finds any of that, let him sprinkle his private part - meaning wash it - and perform wudu."
"6","Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Marwazi narrated to us in Baghdad, Abu Bakr - meaning Ibn Ayyash - narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was a man who emitted much madhy, and I was too shy to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because his daughter was married to me, so I ordered a man and he asked him, and he said: From it is wudu."
"7","Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Hizam ibn Hakim, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Sa'd, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: As for water after water, it is madhy, and every stallion emits madhy, so wash your private part and your testicles from that and perform your wudu for prayer."
"8","(5) Chapter on what is reported about wudu from vomiting. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from his father, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from al-Awza'i, from Ya'ish, from his father, from Ma'dan ibn Talhah, from Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) vomited and broke his fast. He said: So I met Thawban in the mosque of Damascus and mentioned that to him, and he said: He spoke the truth, I poured the wudu water for him."
"9","(6) Chapter on wudu from sleep. Ibn al-Muqri, Abdullah ibn Hashim and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you wakes from sleep, let him not dip his hand into his wudu water until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night. Ibn al-Muqri once said: where his hand spent the night. This wording is Ibn al-Muqri's."
"10","Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, he heard Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I spent the night at my aunt Maymunah's, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rise at night to a water-skin, take water from it and perform a light wudu, making it brief. He said: So I did the same as he did, and I stood on his left, and he moved me to his right, then he prayed as long as Allah willed, then he slept until he snored, then the caller came to him, and he rose for prayer and did not perform wudu."
"11","Muhammad ibn Yahya and Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I spent the night at my aunt Maymunah bint al-Harith's, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose at night to pray, then he lay down and slept until he snored. He said: Then Bilal came to him and announced the prayer, and he rose and prayed and did not perform wudu."
"12","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My eyes sleep but my heart does not sleep."
"13","(7) Purification for one who faints. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Abi A'ishah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, he said: I entered upon A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and said to her: Will you not narrate to me about the illness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became gravely ill and said: Have the people prayed? We said: No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Put water for me in the wash-basin. So we did. She said: So he performed ghusl, then he went to rise and fainted, then he recovered and said: Have the people prayed? We said: No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Put water for me in the wash-basin. So we did. She said: So he performed ghusl, then he went to rise and fainted, then he recovered and said: Have the people prayed? We said: No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Put water for me in the wash-basin. So we did. So he performed ghusl, then he went to rise and fainted, then he recovered and said: Have the people prayed? We said: No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of Allah. She said: And the people were gathered in the mosque waiting for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the last Isha prayer. She said: So he sent to Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer."
"14","(8) Purification of a polytheist when he embraces Islam. Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Agharr, from Khalifah ibn Husayn ibn Qays ibn Asim, from his grandfather Qays ibn Asim: that he embraced Islam, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to perform ghusl with water and sidr."
"15","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah and Abdullah, sons of Umar, narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him: that Thumamah al-Hanafi was captured, then he embraced Islam, and he ordered him to perform ghusl, so he performed ghusl and prayed two rak'ahs, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother's Islam has indeed become good."
"16","(9) Wudu from touching the penis. Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, he said: My father and Urwah discussed what requires wudu, and Urwah mentioned, until he mentioned wudu from touching the penis. My father said: I never heard of it. He said: Marwan informed me, from Busrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever touches his penis, let him perform wudu. We said: Send to her. So he sent a guard or a man, and the messenger returned with that confirmed."
"17","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Marwan, from Busrah bint Safwan, that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If one of you touches his penis, let him perform wudu."
"18","Abu al-Azhar Ahmad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Rabi'ah ibn Uthman, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Marwan, from Busrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever touches his penis, let him perform wudu. Urwah said: I asked Busrah and she confirmed it."
"19","Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: al-Zubaydi narrated to me, he said: Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any man who touches his private part, let him perform wudu, and any woman who touches her private part, let her perform wudu."
"20","(10) What is reported about dropping wudu for it. Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about touching the penis, and he did not see any wudu in it."
"21","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Badr narrated to me, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father, he said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came, as if a Bedouin, and said: O Prophet of Allah, what do you think about a man touching his penis in prayer? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Is it but a piece of flesh - or he said: a part - of you?"
"22","(11) What is reported about leaving wudu for what fire has touched. Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Hisham - meaning Ibn Urwah - he said: Wahb ibn Kaysan narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, (ح)."
"23","He said: And Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, (ح)."
"24","He said: And al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, (ح)."
"25","He said: And al-Zuhri narrated to me, he said: So-and-so ibn Amr ibn Umayyah narrated to me, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate meat or a bone with meat, then prayed and did not touch water."
"26","Muhammad ibn Awf al-Ta'i, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh and Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Himsi narrated to us, they said: Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The last of the two matters from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leaving wudu for what fire has touched. Ibn Awf said: from Shu'ayb, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir."
"27","(12) Wudu from camel meat. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ja'far ibn Abi Thawr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Should I perform wudu from mutton? He said: No. He said: May I pray in sheep pens? He said: Yes. He said: Should I perform wudu from camel meat? He said: Yes. He said: May I pray in camel resting places? He said: No."
"28","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhadir al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara ibn Azib, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: May I pray in camel resting places? He said: No. He said: Should I perform wudu from their meat? He said: Yes. He said: May I pray in sheep folds? He said: Yes. He said: Should I perform wudu from their meat? He said: No. Abu Muhammad said: And Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab and Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha narrated it from Ja'far ibn Abi Thawr."
"29","(13) What is reported about going far for relieving oneself. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad - meaning Ibn Amr - narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, and when he went to relieve himself he would go far off the path."
"30","(14) What is said upon entering the lavatory. Abu Ja'far Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz - meaning Ibn Suhayb - narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered the lavatory, would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from male and female devils."
"31","(15) Dislike of facing the qiblah for stool and urine and cleaning oneself. Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah, Waki and Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us - Yusuf said: and the wording is al-Darir's - they said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: It was said to Salman: Your Prophet has taught you everything, even defecation. He said: Yes, he has forbidden us to face the qiblah with stool or urine, or to clean ourselves with our right hands, or for one of us to be alone with fewer than three stones, and that none of us clean himself with dung or bone."
"32","Abu Sa'id Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Uqbah - meaning Ibn Khalid - narrated to me, he said: Ubaydullah, meaning Ibn Umar, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban narrated to me, from Wasi ibn Habban, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I climbed above Hafsah's house and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) relieving himself facing Bayt al-Maqdis and turning his back to the Ka'bah."
"33","Abu al-Azhar Ahmad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub, meaning Ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Aban ibn Salih narrated to me, from Mujahid ibn Jabr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had forbidden us to turn our backs to the qiblah or face it with our private parts when we urinate. Then he said: I saw him, a year before his death, urinating facing the qiblah."
"34","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan, from Marwan al-Asfar, he said: I saw Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, make his camel kneel facing the qiblah, then sit urinating toward it. I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, has this not been forbidden? He said: Yes, but that was forbidden only in open land; if there is something between you and the qiblah screening you, there is no harm."
"35","(16) Places to be avoided for stool and urine. al-Rabi ibn Sulayman narrated to us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Sulayman, meaning Ibn Bilal, informed me, from al-Ala, he narrated from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Avoid the two cursed things! They said: What are the two cursed ones, O Messenger of Allah? He said: One who defecates on people's road or in a gathering of people."
"36","Abu Ja'far al-Mukharrimi Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us. ح. And Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you urinate in a hole. This is Ishaq's wording, and he added: They said to Qatadah: What is disliked about urinating in a hole? He said: It is said they are dwellings of the jinn."
"37","Muhammad ibn Yahya and Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you urinate in his washing place, for most whisperings come from it."
"38","(17) Permission to urinate standing and near people. Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he came to a refuse heap of a people and urinated standing. So I stepped aside, and he called me and said: Why did you step aside? So I stood at his heels, and when he finished he called for water and performed wudu and wiped over his leather socks."
"39","(18) Dislike of greeting one who is urinating. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Sa'id, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr, that is Ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, narrated to me, from Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: that a man passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was passing water, and the man greeted him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned the greeting to him, then said: If you see me like this, do not greet me, for if you do, I will not return the greeting to you."
"40","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Qabisah and Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A man passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was urinating and greeted him, and he did not return the greeting to him."
"41","(19) Preference for odd numbers in cleaning oneself. Muhammad ibn Yahya and Abu Ja'far al-Darimi narrated to us, they said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you performs wudu, let him put water in his nose then blow it out, and whoever cleans himself with stones, let him do odd numbers."
"42","(20) Cleaning oneself with water. Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Bayruti informed us that Ibn Shu'ayb informed him, he said: Utbah ibn Abi Hakim al-Hamdani informed me, from Talhah ibn Nafi, that he narrated to him, he said: Abu Ayyub, Jabir ibn Abdullah and Anas ibn Malik, the Ansaris, narrated to me that when this verse was revealed: In it are men who love to purify themselves, and Allah loves those who purify themselves - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of Ansar, Allah has praised you well for purification, so what is this purification of yours? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we perform wudu for prayer and ghusl from janabah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is there anything else with that? They said: No, except that when one of us comes out from relieving himself he likes to clean himself with water. He said: That is it, so keep to it."
"43","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go to relieve himself, and I and a boy of ours would follow him with a water-skin, and when he finished his need I would hand him the water-skin and he would clean himself."
"44","(21) What is said upon leaving the lavatory. Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn al-Qasim informed us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, he said: A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, narrated to me: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came out from relieving himself, would say: Your forgiveness."
"45","(22) On the purity of water and the amount that becomes impure and does not. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Sa'id ibn Salamah, that al-Mughirah ibn Abi Burdah informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, say: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we ride the sea and carry little water with us; if we perform wudu with it we thirst - so may we perform wudu with seawater? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Its water is purifying, its dead is lawful."
"46","Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Warraq, Hajjaj ibn Hamzah al-Wazi and Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Attar narrated to us, they said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Ja'far, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about water and what predators and beasts frequent of it, and he said: If water is two qullahs, it does not carry impurity."
"47","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, (ح). And Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Qirati narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked similarly. And Isa ibn Yunus said, from al-Walid, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father. And Muhammad ibn Ishaq said, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father likewise."
"48","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn al-Mundhir informed me, he said: We were in a garden of ours or of Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, and prayer came, so Ubaydullah stood toward the garden's water channel, in which was a camel skin, and began to perform wudu from it. We said: Do you perform wudu from this when there is a camel skin in it? He said: My father narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If water is two qullahs, it does not become impure."
"49","Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Warraq and Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, they said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah - al-Masruqi said: ibn Rafi ibn Khadij - from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, may we perform wudu from the well of Buda'ah? And it is a well into which filth, menstrual cloths and dog meat are thrown. He said: Water is pure, nothing makes it impure."
"50","Muhammad ibn Yahya, Ahmad ibn Yusuf and Ibn Awn narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to one of his wives when there was leftover from her ghusl or her wudu, and he wanted to perform wudu with it, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, I performed ghusl from it from janabah. He said: Water does not become impure."
"51","Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: al-Thawri informed us with this chain similarly."
"52","Muhammad ibn Yahya and Abu Ja'far al-Darimi narrated to us, they said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a dog drinks from the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times."
"53","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn al-Khalil narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mushir informed us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Razin and Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him pour it out and wash it seven times."
"54","Ali ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If a dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times."
"55","And Ayyub said: from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the first of them or one of them with dust."
"56","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Mutarrif, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a dog laps in a vessel, wash it seven times, and the eighth time rub it with dust."
"57","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him. And from Hammam ibn Munabbih, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let none of you urinate in stagnant water that does not flow, then perform wudu from it."
"58","Muhammad ibn Yahya and Allan ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, they said: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad - that is Ibn Ja'far - and Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, they said: Utbah - that is Ibn Muslim - narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn Hunayn, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If a fly falls into the drink of one of you, let him dip all of it, then throw it out, for in one of its wings is disease and in the other is cure."
"59","Bahr ibn Nasr informed us, from Ibn Wahb, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah, that Abu al-Sa'ib narrated to him, that he heard Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you perform ghusl in stagnant water while he is junub. He said: How should he do it, O Abu Hurayrah? He said: He should take from it handful by handful."
"60","Ibn al-Muqri and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ghusl with a cup, and I and he would perform ghusl from one vessel. Mahmud added: and it is the faraq."
"61","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Men and women used to perform wudu in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from one vessel all together."
"62","Muhammad ibn Yahya informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Humayd informed us, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw spittle in the qiblah of the mosque and scraped it with his hand, and the severity of that upon him was seen in his face, and he said: When a servant stands to pray, he is but conversing with his Lord - or his Lord is between him and the qiblah - so if one of you spits, let him spit to his left or under his foot, or do like this - and he spat into his garment and rubbed part of it against part."
"63","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: I read to Abdullah ibn Nafi, and Mutarrif ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Malik, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Humaydah bint Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah, from Kabshah bint Ka'b ibn Malik - and she was married to Ibn Abi Qatadah - that Abu Qatadah entered upon her and she poured wudu water for him, then a cat came drinking from it, so he tilted the vessel for it until it drank. Kabshah said: He saw me looking at him, and he said: Are you surprised, O daughter of my brother? She said: I said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not impure; it is among those that go around you, male or female."
"64","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid and Ahmad ibn Shayban al-Ramli narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Wa'lah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, in marfu' form - and Ibn al-Muqri said once: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - : Any skin that is tanned has become pure. And Ibn Shayban said: He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said."
"65","Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Isma'il Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, he said: Abu Rayhanah narrated to us, from Safinah, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ghusl with a sa' and perform wudu with a mudd."
"66","(23) What is reported about the siwak. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would burden my ummah, I would have ordered them to use the siwak with every wudu."
"67","(24) On intention in deeds. Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Alqamah ibn Waqqas, he said: I heard Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, on the pulpit informing that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Actions are by intention, and every man has what he intends; whoever's hijrah is to Allah and His Messenger, his hijrah is to what he migrated to, and whoever's hijrah is to a worldly thing he attains or a woman he marries, his hijrah is to what he migrated to."
"68","(25) No prayer is accepted without purification. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, he said: People began praising Ibn Amir at his death, so Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: I am not the least sincere of them to you, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from embezzlement."
"69","Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq ibn Hammam narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, he said: This is what Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us, from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of one of you is not accepted when he breaks wudu until he performs wudu."
"70","(26) Description of the wudu of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and what he ordered. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Humran ibn Aban, he said: I saw Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, perform wudu: he poured over his hands three times and washed them, then rinsed his mouth and blew out his nose three times, then washed his face three times, then washed his right hand to the elbow three times, then the left likewise [then wiped his head, then washed his right foot to the ankles three times, then the left likewise], then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform wudu like this wudu of mine, then he said: Whoever performs wudu like this wudu of mine, then prays two rak'ahs not conversing with himself in them, is forgiven what preceded of his sin."
"71","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, he said: Za'idah ibn Qudamah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Alqamah al-Hamdani, from Abd Khayr, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, entered the courtyard after praying Fajr and sat in the courtyard, then said to a boy of his: Bring me purifying water. The boy brought him a vessel with water and a basin. Abd Khayr said - and we were sitting looking at him: He took the vessel with his right and poured over his left hand, then washed his palms, then took the vessel with his right hand and poured over his left hand, then washed his palms, then took the vessel with his right hand and poured over his left hand, then washed his palms, doing it three times. Abd Khayr said: All of that he would not put his hand into the vessel until he had washed it three times. Then he put his right hand into the vessel and filled his mouth, rinsed his mouth, sniffed water and blew it out with his left hand three times, then washed his face three times, then washed his right hand three times to the elbow, then washed his left hand three times to the elbow, then put his right hand into the vessel until the water covered it, then raised it with what it carried of water, then wiped it with his left hand, then wiped his head with both his hands together once, then put his right hand into the vessel, then poured over his right foot and washed it three times with his left hand, then put his right hand into the vessel and filled it with water, then drank from it, then said: This is the purification of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); whoever wishes to look at the purification of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), this is his purification."
"72","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: al-Thawri, Ma'mar and Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu once each."
"73","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu: he washed his hands twice, his feet twice and his face three times."
"74","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih ibn Muslim al-Ijli narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I sometimes saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform wudu twice each."
"75","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, informed us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Amir ibn Shaqiq, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, he said: I saw Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, perform wudu: he washed his palms three times, rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, washed his face three times, wiped his head and his ears, their outer and inner, washed his feet three times each, ran his fingers between his toes and through his beard, until he had washed his face three times each. And he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do as you saw me do. It was said to Ishaq: Is there not in it: and washed his forearms? He said: What I had with me, I gave you."
"76","And Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated it to us, he said: Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us with this chain, and he said in it: and washed his forearms three times."
"77","Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Ibn Wahb, from Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Salim and Malik ibn Anas, from Amr ibn Yahya al-Mazini, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Asim al-Mazini, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he poured from the vessel onto his hands and washed them, rinsed his mouth and blew out his nose three times, and that he took water with his hands and began with the front of his head, then went with his hands to the back of the head, then returned them to the front."
"78","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Hariz ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maysarah al-Hadrami narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Wudu water was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he performed wudu three times each, then wiped his head and his ears, their outer and inner."
"79","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Musa ibn Abi A'ishah, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather: that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about wudu, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu three times each and said: Whoever adds has done wrong, transgressed, overstepped and wronged."
"80","Ibn al-Muqri and Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you performs wudu, let him put water in his nose, then blow it out."
"81","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Qariz ibn Shaybah, from Abu Ghatfan, he said: I entered upon Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, and found him performing wudu: he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, then said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blow out your noses two thorough times or three."
"82","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Shu'bah, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, would pass by us while people performed wudu from the ablution vessel, and I heard him say: Perform wudu fully, for I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"83","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, (ح). And Abu Ja'far al-Darimi narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr narrated to us, both from Shu'bah with this: Muhammad said: for the heel, and the other said: for the heels."
"84","al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulaym al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Kathir narrated to me, from Asim ibn Laqit ibn Sabirah, from his father, I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about wudu. He said: Perform wudu fully, run water between the fingers, and exaggerate in sniffing water, unless you are fasting."
"85","(27) Chapter on wiping over leather socks. Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, he said: I saw Jarir perform wudu from an ablution vessel and wipe over his leather socks. They said: Do you wipe over your leather socks? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do it. He said: This hadith used to please the companions of Abdullah, saying: His Islam was only after the revelation of al-Ma'idah."
"86","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Bukayr, meaning Ibn Amir al-Bajali, narrated to us, from Abu Zur'ah, he said: Jarir urinated and wiped over the leather socks, and people criticized him, saying: This was before al-Ma'idah. He said: I only embraced Islam after al-Ma'idah was revealed, and I only saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe after it was revealed."
"87","Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Bakr, from al-Hasan, from Ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from his father - Bakr said: and we heard it from Ibn al-Mughirah, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu and wiped over his forelock, over the turban and over the leather socks."
"88","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Amr al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Raja ibn Haywah, from the scribe of al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped the top of the leather sock and its bottom."
"89","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe over the backs of the leather socks."
"90","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam and Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night, for wiping over leather socks."
"91","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Muhajir ibn Makhlad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed for the resident a day and a night, and for the traveler three days and their nights, for wiping over leather socks."
"92","(28) On janabah and purification for it. Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Waki narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, from her mother, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about a woman who sees in a dream what a man sees. He said: If she sees water, let her perform ghusl. She said: I said: You have disgraced women - does a woman have a wet dream? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May your right hand be dusty - then how does her child resemble her?"
"93","al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Khalid al-Khayyat narrated to us, from Abdullah al-Umari, from Ubaydullah, from al-Qasim, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who finds wetness and does not remember a wet dream? He said: He performs ghusl. And about a man who thinks he had a wet dream and finds no wetness? He said: No ghusl upon him."
"94","Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Attar and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Khalid with this chain similarly, and he added: Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of Allah, is there anything upon a woman who sees something of that? He said: Yes, women are the counterparts of men."
"95","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Men of the Ansar, among them Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and Abu Ayyub, used to say: Water is from water, claiming that one who touches his wife has no ghusl unless he ejaculates. When that was mentioned to Umar, A'ishah and Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, they rejected it and said: If the two circumcised parts meet, ghusl has become obligatory. Sahl al-Ansari, who had met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was fifteen years old in his time, said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me that the fatwa they used to give - water is from water - was a concession the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted at the beginning of Islam, then he ordered ghusl afterwards. And Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan had taken that from a man of the Ansar, but when knowledge reached him he performed ghusl and ordered ghusl."
"96","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith and Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, they said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [TRUNCATED in print: text breaks off here; continued in no. 97.]"
"97","He said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed me, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: When he sits between her four parts and then exerts himself..."
"98","And 'Abd al-Samad and Abu Nu'aym said: ""...then he strives with her - ghusl has become obligatory."""
"99","Sulayman ibn Shu'ayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Bishr - meaning Ibn Bakr - narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to me, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, from his father, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she was asked about a man who has intercourse but does not ejaculate. She said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I did that, and we both performed ghusl from it. And al-Walid ibn Muslim also raised it (to the Prophet)."
"100","'Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: 'Amr ibn Murrah narrated to me, from 'Abdullah ibn Salamah, he said: I came to 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, I and two men of my people and a man of Banu Asad - I think - and he sent the two of them off on some errand. He said: You two are stout men, so strive for your religion. Then he entered the lavatory and prepared himself, then came out and took a basin of water and wiped himself with it, then began to recite, and it was as if we disapproved. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would relieve himself, then come out and recite the Qur'an, and we would eat meat with him, and nothing would prevent him from that except janabah. Yahya said: And Shu'bah used to say regarding this hadith: Do you recognize and disapprove? - meaning that 'Abdullah ibn Salamah had grown old by the time 'Amr met him."
"101","'Abdullah ibn Hashim and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: May one of us sleep while he is junub? He said: Let him perform wudu, then sleep, and eat if he wishes."
"102","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Humayd narrated to us, from Bakr, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met him while he was junub. He said: So I slipped away and performed ghusl, then I came, and he said: Where were you? I said: I was junub. He said: The Muslim does not become impure."
"103","Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb, from Ibn 'Abbas, from Maymunah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I screened the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he performed ghusl from janabah."
"104","Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from 'Abdullah ibn Rafi', the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who braids her hair tightly; should I undo it for ghusl from janabah? He said: It suffices you to pour three handfuls of water over it, then pour water over yourself, and you will be purified - or he said: then you will have become purified."
"105","'Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: My father informed me, he said: 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, informed me about the ghusl of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from janabah. She said: He would begin with his hands and wash them, then perform his wudu for prayer, then run his fingers through the roots of his head hair, until when he thought he had reached the skin, he would scoop three scoops and pour them over his head, then pour water over the rest of his body."
"106","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Salim, from Kurayb, from Ibn 'Abbas, from Maymunah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ghusl: he washed his private part and rubbed his hand on the ground - or he said: on the wall - then performed his wudu for prayer, then poured water over his head and the rest of his body, then stepped aside and washed his feet. I handed him a cloth to dry himself with - or to wipe with - but he refused to take it, and gestured with his hand like this, shaking it off."
"107","(29) Chapter on Menstruation. 'Ali ibn Khashram informed us that Isma'il Ibn 'Ulayyah informed them, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Mu'adhah al-'Adawiyyah, she said: A woman asked 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her: Should a menstruating woman make up the prayers? She said: Are you a Haruriyyah? We used to menstruate in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we would not make up (the prayers), nor would we be commanded to make them up."
"108","Muhammad ibn Yahya and Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, they said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-A'mash, from Thabit ibn 'Ubayd, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hand me the mat - while she was menstruating. She said: I am menstruating. He said: It is not in your hand."
"109","Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from his mother, she said: I heard 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would place his head in the lap of one of us while she was menstruating and recite the Qur'an."
"110","'Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would bring his head near me while he was in retreat, and I would wash it and comb it while I was in my room - and I was menstruating - while he was in the mosque."
"111","Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us through him (the same chain) another time, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Umm 'Atiyyah, he said: It was mentioned to her and she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Bring out the young unmarried women and the secluded ones to witness the 'Eid and the supplication of the Muslims, and let the menstruating women keep away from the prayer-place of the Muslims."
"112","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: When I menstruated, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would order me to wrap my waist-wrapper, and he would embrace me."
"113","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hakim al-Athram, from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Whoever goes to a soothsayer and believes what he says, or approaches a woman in her back passage, or approaches a menstruating woman, has disavowed what was revealed to Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"114","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from 'Abd al-Hamid, from Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said regarding one who approaches his wife while she is menstruating: He should give a dinar or half a dinar in charity."
"115","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn 'Amir narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from 'Abd al-Hamid, from Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, likewise. Shu'bah said: And so-and-so and so-and-so claimed that al-Hakam did not raise it (to the Prophet). It was said to Shu'bah: Narrate to us what you heard and leave the statement of so-and-so and so-and-so. He said: It would not please me to live in this world the lifespan of Nuh while narrating this or staying silent about it."
"116","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Bundar narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us with this hadith, and he did not raise it (to the Prophet). A man said to Shu'bah: You used to raise it? He said: I was mad, then I recovered."
"117","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Sa'id - meaning Ibn Abi 'Arubah - narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Karim, from Miqsam, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He should give a dinar or half a dinar in charity."
"118","Muhammad ibn Yahya and Abu Ja'far al-Darimi narrated to us, they said: Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah informed us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who suffers prolonged bleeding and never becomes pure; should I abandon prayer? He said: No, that is only a vein and is not menstruation. When menstruation comes, leave prayer; and when it departs, wash the blood from yourself and pray."
"119","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah, from Nafi', from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that a man informed him, from Umm Salamah, that a woman suffered continuous flowing blood that did not stop. Umm Salamah asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Let her consider the number of days and nights she used to menstruate before that, and let her leave prayer for that amount; then when the prayer time comes, let her perform ghusl, wrap herself with a cloth, and pray. Abu Muhammad said: Musa ibn 'Uqbah and al-Layth ibn Sa'd said likewise, from Nafi', from Sulayman, from a man, from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her. And Malik, 'Ubaydullah, Yahya ibn Sa'id and others said: from Nafi', from Sulayman, from Umm Salamah. And Ayyub said: from Sulayman himself, from Umm Salamah."
"120","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from 'Irak, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: Umm Habibah bint Jahsh, who was married to 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, complained to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about bleeding. He said to her: Remain for the duration your menstruation used to confine you, then perform ghusl. She said: And she used to perform ghusl for every prayer."
"121","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, he said: Zaynab bint Umm Salamah informed me that a woman suffered flowing blood, and she was married to 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded her to perform ghusl for every prayer and pray. And Ma'mar and Hisham narrated it, saying: from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, that Umm Habibah..."
"122","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Shayban, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Abi Bakr, that she informed him that 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said regarding a woman who sees something suspicious after purification: It is only a vein, or veins."
"123","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: A woman of the Ansar asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about a menstruating woman when she wishes to perform ghusl from menstruation. He said: Take your water and lote-leaves, then perform ghusl and cleanse well, then pour over your head until you reach the roots of the head, then take a musk-scented piece of cloth. She said: How should I do it? He fell silent. Then she said: How should I do it? He fell silent. 'A'ishah said: Take a musk-scented piece of cloth and follow the traces of blood with it - while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, listened and did not object to her."
"124","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yunus ibn 'Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from 'Uthman ibn Abi al-'As, that he would not approach women for forty days - meaning during postpartum bleeding. Abu Muhammad said: And Abu Bakr al-Hudhali reported it as a chain reaching back, from al-Hasan."
"125","Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A woman in postpartum bleeding refrains from prayer for forty days."
"126","Ibn al-Muqri' and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir, from her grandmother Asma': that a woman asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about a garment struck by menstrual blood. He said: Scrape it, rub it, sprinkle it with water, and pray."
"127","(30) Chapter on Tayammum. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah narrated to me, from Ibn 'Abbas, from 'Ammar ibn Yasir, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, halted for the night at Dhat al-Jaysh, accompanied by 'A'ishah, his wife. A necklace of hers made of Zafari onyx beads broke, and the people were detained searching for that necklace until dawn broke, with no water with them. Abu Bakr became angry with her and said: You have detained the people, and they have no water. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, then sent down upon His Messenger the concession of purification with clean earth. The Muslims rose with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, struck the ground with their hands, then raised their hands without taking any dust, and wiped their faces and their arms up to the shoulders, and the inner parts of their hands up to the armpits. Ibn Shihab said: But people do not follow this (in full)."
"128","'Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Awf narrated to us, he said: Abu Raja' narrated to us, he said: 'Imran ibn Husayn narrated to me, he said: We were on a journey with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he led the people in prayer. When he finished his prayer, he saw a man standing apart who had not prayed with the people. He said: What prevented you, O so-and-so, from praying with the people? He said: O Messenger of Allah, janabah befell me and there is no water. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Clean earth is incumbent upon you, for it suffices you."
"129","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad - meaning Ibn 'Amr - narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The earth has been made for me a mosque and a means of purification."
"130","Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj al-Anmati narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every good land has been made for me a mosque and a means of purification."
"131","'Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Shu'bah, he said: al-Hakam narrated to me, from Dharr, from Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father: that a man came to 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: I became junub and found no water. He said: Do not pray. 'Ammar said: Do you not remember, O Commander of the Believers, when you and I were on an expedition and we became junub and found no water? As for you, you did not pray, but as for me, I rolled in the dust and prayed. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It would have sufficed you to strike the ground with your hands, then blow, then wipe your face and hands with them. 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Fear Allah, O 'Ammar. He said: If you wish, I will not narrate it."
"132","Al-Hakam said: And Ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza narrated it to me, from his father, like the hadith of Dharr."
"133","He said: And Salamah narrated to me, from Dharr, in this chain which al-Hakam mentioned, he said: 'Umar said: Rather, we entrust you with what you have undertaken."
"134","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Aban al-'Attar narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from 'Azrah, from Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from 'Ammar ibn Yasir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say regarding tayammum: One strike for the face and the hands."
"135","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to me, he said: Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, from 'Umayr, the freedman of Ibn 'Abbas, that he heard him say: I came, I and 'Abdullah ibn Yasar, the freedman of Maymunah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until we entered upon Abu al-Juhaym ibn al-Harith ibn al-Simmah al-Ansari. Abu al-Juhaym said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came from the direction of Bi'r Jamal, when a man met him and greeted him. The Messenger of Allah did not return the greeting until he went to a wall and wiped his face and hands."
"136","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rabah informed me that 'Ata' narrated to him, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a man became junub in winter and asked, and was ordered to perform ghusl; he performed ghusl and died. That was mentioned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: How did they kill him - may Allah kill them - three times. Allah has made the earth, or tayammum, a means of purification - Ibn 'Abbas was uncertain, then affirmed it afterwards."
"137","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to me, he said: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, raising it (to the Prophet), regarding His saying, Exalted is He: And if you are ill or on a journey - he said: When a man has wounds sustained in the path of Allah, or sores, or smallpox, and becomes junub, and fears that if he performs ghusl he will die, let him perform tayammum."
"138","(31) On keeping bodies and clothes free of impurities. al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, he said: I heard Mujahid narrating from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by two graves and said: They are being punished, and they are not being punished for something grave: as for this one, he used to spread tale-bearing, and as for this other, he would not guard himself against his urine. Then he called for a moist palm-stalk, split it in two, planted one on this one and one on this one, then said: Perhaps it will lighten for them so long as they do not dry out."
"139","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hasanah, he said: I and 'Amr ibn al-'As were sitting when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us with a shield in his hand. He urinated while seated, and we spoke among ourselves, saying: He urinates as a woman urinates. He came to us and said: Do you not know what befell a man of the Children of Israel? When urine touched them, they would cut it off, and he forbade them, and he was punished in his grave."
"140","Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Ibn Wahb, from Ibn Lahi'ah, al-Layth ibn Sa'd and 'Amr ibn al-Harith, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Mu'awiyah ibn Hudayj, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I asked Umm Habibah - wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, may Allah be pleased with her: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray in the garment in which he was intimate with her? She said: Yes, so long as he saw no harm in it."
"141","Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from Maymunah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in a woolen cloak, part of it over her while she was menstruating."
"142","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to me, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: al-Ash'ath narrated to us, from Muhammad, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq al-'Uqayli, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not pray in the blankets of his wives."
"143","Muhammad ibn Yahya and Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, they said: Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, he said: There was a guest with 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who became junub and began washing what had touched him. 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to order us to scrape it off."
"144","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I used to rub it from the garment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he would pray in it. I said to al-Ansari: Do you mean janabah? He said: What else?"
"145","al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: 'Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Hammad informed us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I used to rub semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he would pray in it."
"146","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Yasar narrated to me, he said: 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, informed me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when semen touched his garment, would wash what had touched it, then go out to prayer while I looked at the spots on his garment from the washing."
"147","Ibn al-Muqri' and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah, from Umm Qays, she said: I entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a son of mine who had not yet eaten food. He urinated on him, so he called for water and sprinkled it. And Ma'mar, al-Layth and 'Amr ibn al-Harith said, from al-Zuhri regarding this: So he splashed it."
"148","Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: Boys used to be brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he might supplicate for them. A boy urinated on him, and he followed up the urine with water."
"149","Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah: that a Bedouin entered the mosque and prayed. When he finished, he said: O Allah, have mercy on me and Muhammad, and have mercy on no one with us. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned to him and said: You have constricted what is vast. Before long he urinated in the mosque, and the people hastened to him, but he forbade them, saying: Pour over it a bucket or a pail of water - meaning his urine - and said: You were sent as facilitators and were not sent as those who make things difficult."
"150","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Umarah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from a freedwoman of Ibrahim ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, she said: I would lengthen my train, passing through filthy places and clean places. I entered upon Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and asked her about that. She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: What comes after it purifies it."
"151","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr and Sharik narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Isa ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Musa ibn 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from a woman of Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal, that she asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: We have foul-smelling roads, and it rains. He said: Is there not after it a road purer than it? She said: Yes. He said: Then this is for that."
"152","(32) On the obligation of the five prayers and their discussions. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: And among what I read to 'Abdullah ibn Nafi', and Mutarrif narrated to me, from Malik, from his uncle Abu Suhayl ibn Malik, from his father, that he heard Talhah ibn 'Ubaydullah, may Allah be pleased with him, say: A man of Najd came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with dishevelled head, his loud voice heard but his words not understood, until he drew near and asked about Islam. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Five prayers in the day and night. He said: Is there any other upon me? He said: No, unless you volunteer. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And fasting the month of Ramadan. He said: Is there any other upon me? He said: No, unless you volunteer. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned zakah to him. He said: Is there any other upon me? He said: No, unless you volunteer. He said: The man turned away saying: I will neither add to this nor diminish from it. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He will succeed if he is truthful."
"153","'Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah and Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, that they heard Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I prayed Zhuhr with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Madinah, four (rak'ahs), and I prayed 'Asr with him at Dhu al-Hulayfah, two rak'ahs."
"154","'Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah - meaning Ibn Idris - narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi 'Ammar, from 'Abdullah ibn Babah, from Ya'la ibn Umayyah, he said: I said to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him: There is no blame upon you to shorten prayer if you fear - yet the people are safe. 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I wondered at what you wondered at, so I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: It is a charity with which Allah has been charitable to you, so accept His charity."
"155","Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Mallas al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Harmalah ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Juhani narrated to us in the year 192, he said: My uncle 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Rabi' narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Command the boy to pray at seven years, and strike him for it at ten."
"156","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet, who said: The pen has been lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, from the child until he grows up, and from the insane until he becomes sane or recovers."
"157","Muhammad narrated to us, from 'Affan with this (chain), and he said: Until he reaches puberty."
"158","(33) On the prayer times. Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, he said: Hakim ibn Hakim narrated to me, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Jibril, peace be upon him, led me at the House: he led me in Zhuhr when the sun declined, when it was the measure of a sandal-strap; then he led me in 'Asr when the shadow of everything was its like; then he led me in Maghrib when the fasting person breaks fast; then he led me in 'Isha' when the twilight disappeared; then he led me in Fajr when food and drink became forbidden to the fasting person. Then he led me the next day in Zhuhr when the shadow of everything was its like; then he led me in 'Asr when the shadow of everything was twice its like; then he led me in Maghrib when the fasting person breaks fast, at one time; then he led me in 'Isha' up to the first third of the night; then he led me in Fajr and brightened it. Then he turned to me and said: O Muhammad, this is the time of the prophets before you, and the time is between these two times."
"159","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym and Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Hakim ibn Hakim ibn 'Abbad ibn Hunayf, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Jibril, peace be upon him, led me at the House twice. Ibn Yahya said: And both narrated the hadith together, mentioning prayer at two times, in hastening and in brightening."
"160","Muhammad ibn Bazi' al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq - meaning Ibn Yusuf al-Azraq - informed us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from 'Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and asked him about the prayer time. He said: Pray these two with us. He ordered Bilal when the sun declined, and he called the adhan; then he ordered him and he established Zhuhr; then he ordered him and he established 'Asr while the sun was high, white and clear; then he ordered him and he established Maghrib when the sun set; then he ordered him and he established 'Isha' when the twilight disappeared; then he ordered him and he established Fajr when dawn broke. The next day he ordered him to cool Zhuhr, and he was generous in cooling it; then he ordered him and he established - meaning 'Asr - while the sun was higher than before; then he ordered him and he established Maghrib before the twilight disappeared; then he ordered him and he established 'Isha' when a third of the night had gone; then he ordered him and he established Fajr and brightened it. Then he said: Where is the questioner about the prayer time? The man stood up to him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your prayer time is between what you have seen."
"161","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever catches a rak'ah of 'Asr before the sun sets has caught it, and whoever catches a rak'ah of Subh before the sun rises has caught it."
"162","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Tarkhan narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Sulayman - meaning Ibn al-Mughirah - narrated to us, from Thabit, from 'Abdullah ibn Rabah, from Abu Qatadah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: There is no negligence in sleep; negligence is only upon one who does not pray a prayer until the time of the next prayer comes."
"163","'Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Abu 'Uthman, from Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let not the adhan of Bilal - or he said: the call of Bilal, al-Taymi was uncertain - deceive you, for dawn is not the one that says like this - and he raised his hand - but dawn is the one like this, and he spread his two fingers horizontally."
"164","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn 'Adi narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Whoever catches a prostration of 'Asr prayer before the sun sets, and of Fajr before the sun rises, has caught it."
"165","Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the heat intensifies, cool the prayer, for intense heat is from the exhalation of Hell."
"166","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Hassan, from 'Abidah, from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: They distracted us from the middle prayer, the 'Asr prayer; may Allah fill their graves - or he said: their houses - and their bellies with fire."
"167","(34) On the adhan. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn 'Abd Rabbih, he said: My father 'Abdullah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded the bell to be struck for gathering people for prayer, a man carrying a bell in his hand circled me while I was asleep. I said to him: O servant of Allah, will you sell the bell? He said: What will you do with it? He said: I said: We shall call to prayer with it. He said: Shall I not guide you to what is better than that? I said: Yes. He said: Say: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; come to prayer, come to prayer; come to success, come to success; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah. He said: Then he withdrew a short distance. He said: Then say when you establish prayer: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; come to prayer, come to success; prayer has begun, prayer has begun; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah. When morning came, I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of what I had seen. He said: This is a true dream, Allah willing. Stand with Bilal and cast upon him what you saw, and let him call with it, for he has a more melodious voice than you. I stood with Bilal and began dictating it to him while he called with it. He said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, heard of that while in his house, and came out dragging his cloak, saying: By Him Who sent you with the truth, O Messenger of Allah, I have seen the like of what he was shown. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: To Allah belongs praise."
"168","Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Bilal was commanded to repeat the adhan in pairs and to utter the iqamah singly."
"169","Muhammad ibn Yahya and Muhammad ibn Idris ibn 'Umar narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Simak ibn 'Atiyyah, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Bilal was commanded to repeat the adhan in pairs and to utter the iqamah singly. Ayyub said: Except the iqamah. The wording belongs to Ibn Idris."
"170","Abu Ja'far al-Darimi Ahmad ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Isma'il Ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us, he said: I said to Ayyub: Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Bilal was commanded to repeat the adhan in pairs and to utter the iqamah singly. Ayyub said: Except the iqamah."
"171","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: 'Amir al-Ahwal narrated to us, he said: Makhul narrated to me that Ibn Muhayriz narrated to him that Abu Mahdhurah informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught him the adhan of nineteen phrases and the iqamah of seventeen phrases. The adhan: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; come to prayer, come to prayer; come to success, come to success; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah. And the iqamah: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah; I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; come to prayer, come to prayer; come to success, come to success; prayer has begun, prayer has begun; Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no god but Allah."
"172","Musa ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi and Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Ya'ish narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar."
"173","And from al-Qasim, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Bilal calls at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls."
"174","'Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: 'Isa - meaning Ibn Yunus - informed us, from Shu'bah. And Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far, he said: I heard Aba al-Muthanna, he said: I heard Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: The adhan in the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in pairs, and the iqamah singly, except that he said: Prayer has begun - he repeated it. When we heard it, we would perform wudu and go out to prayer. Abu Muhammad said: Abu al-Muthanna's name is Muslim ibn Mihran, the mu'adhdhin of the Kufah mosque."
"175","(35) On the qiblah. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara', may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he first arrived in Madinah, prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen or seventeen months, though he liked his qiblah to be toward the House (Ka'bah). The first prayer he prayed was 'Asr, and some people prayed with him. A man who had prayed with him went out and passed by people of a mosque bowing, and said: I bear witness by Allah that I prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, toward Makkah. They turned as they were toward the House. And he liked to be turned toward the House; and he mentioned the rest of the hadith."
"176","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, he said: Za'idah ibn Qudamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let one of you place before himself the like of the back of a saddle, and pray."
"177","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: And among what I read to 'Abdullah ibn Nafi', and Mutarrif narrated to me, from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you prays, let him not allow anyone to pass before him, and let him repel him as much as he can; and if he refuses, let him fight him, for he is only a devil."
"178","Ibn al-Muqri' and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah, that he heard Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: I came, I and al-Fadl, on the Day of 'Arafah, while the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was praying, and we were upon a she-ass. We passed before part of the row, dismounted, and left her grazing, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said nothing to us. Mahmud added: So we entered the prayer."
"179","'Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa'id, narrated to me, from Hisham, he said: My father narrated to me, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would pray at night while I lay across between him and the qiblah on the bed. When he wished to pray witr, he would wake me and I would pray witr."
"180","(36) On garments for prayer. 'Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, may a man pray in a single garment? He said: And do all of you find two garments?"
"181","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man to pray in a single garment with nothing of it over his shoulder."
"182","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Mujahid Abu Hazrah, from 'Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn 'Ubadah, he said: I went out, I and my father, until we came to Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, in his mosque - and he mentioned part of the hadith. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood praying. I had a cloak; I tried to cross its ends but it did not reach for me, and it had fringes, so I turned it over, then crossed its ends, then hunched over it. I came and stood to the left of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; he took my hand and turned me until he placed me on his right. Jabbar ibn Sakhr came, performed wudu, then came and stood to the left of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; he took us both by the hands and pushed us until he placed us behind him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, kept glancing at me without my noticing; then I realized. He said: Like this - with his hand, meaning: gird your waist. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished, he said: O Jabir. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: If it is wide, cross its ends; and if it is narrow, tie it over your hips."
"183","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nu'man and Abu al-Walid narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Safiyyah bint al-Harith, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah does not accept the prayer of a menstruating (i.e. adult) woman except with a head-cover."
"184","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Abu Maslamah - he is Sa'id ibn Yazid - he said: I asked Anas, may Allah be pleased with him: Did the Prophet pray in his sandals? He said: Yes."
"185","(37) On the mosque. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah informed me that 'A'ishah and Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, informed him that when the Prophet's, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, (final illness) befell him, he began casting a striped woolen cloth over his face; when distressed he would uncover it from his face, saying: Allah's curse upon the Jews and Christians; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques. 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, says: Warning against what they did."
"186","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Amir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, he said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad narrating from Maymunah: that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray on a small mat."
"187","(38) Description of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Ibn al-Muqri', Harun ibn Ishaq and Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that he saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he began prayer, raise his hands until they were level with his shoulders; and when he wished to bow, and after raising his head from bowing; and he would not raise between the two prostrations."
"188","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: The nephew of Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from his uncle, he said: Salim ibn 'Abdullah informed me that 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he stood for prayer, would raise his hands until they were level with his shoulders and say the takbir; then when he wished to bow, he would raise them until they were level with his shoulders, saying the takbir while they were so, and bow; then when he wished to raise his back, he would raise them until they were level with his shoulders, then say: Allah hears him who praises Him. Then he would prostrate without raising his hands in prostration, and he would raise them in every rak'ah and every takbir he uttered before bowing, until his prayer ended."
"189","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Minhal and Abu Salih, the scribe of al-Layth, both narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, from his uncle al-Majishun ibn Abi Salamah, from al-A'raj, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: that when he began prayer he would say the takbir, then say: I have turned my face to Him Who originated the heavens and the earth, upright, and I am not of the polytheists. My prayer, my sacrifice, my living and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the worlds, with no partner for Him; with that I have been commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the King; there is no god but You. My Lord, and I am Your servant; I have wronged myself and confessed my sin, so forgive me all my sins, for none forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of character, for none guides to its best but You; and turn its evil from me, for none turns its evil from me but You. At Your service and blessed by You; all good is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You; I am by You and to You; Blessed and Exalted are You; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. When he bowed he would say: O Allah, to You I bowed, in You I believed, to You I submitted; my hearing, my sight, my marrow, my bones and my sinews humbled themselves to You. When he raised his head he would say: Allah hears him who praises Him; our Lord, to You belongs praise filling the heavens and the earth, and filling whatever You will besides. When he prostrated he would say: O Allah, to You I prostrated, in You I believed, to You I submitted; my face prostrated to Him Who created it, fashioned it and perfected its form, and opened its hearing and sight; blessed is Allah, the Best of creators. And when he finished his prayer and gave salutations, he would say: O Allah, forgive me what I advanced and what I delayed, what I concealed and what I declared, what I exceeded, and what You know better than I; You are the Advancer and the Delayer; there is no god but You. Abu Salih said in both: I have no god but You."
"190","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Asim al-'Anazi, from Ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered prayer he would say: Allah is Greatest, greatly; praise be to Allah, abundantly - three times; glory be to Allah morning and evening. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan, from his puffing, his spittle and his pricking. 'Amr said: His puffing is arrogance, his pricking is madness, and his spittle is poetry. And Mis'ar said, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from a man of 'Anazah. And there is disagreement from Husayn, from 'Amr ibn Murrah: some said: from 'Ammar ibn 'Asim, and some said: from 'Umarah. And Ibn Idris said: from Husayn, from 'Amr, and from 'Abbad ibn 'Asim."
"191","Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Idris, 'Uqbah and Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I prayed behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr, 'Umar and 'Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them, and they did not recite aloud: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate."
"192","Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Qatadah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, would begin recitation with: Praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"193","204 - Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, and I did not hear them recite aloud ""In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful."" Shu'bah said: I said to Qatadah: Did you yourself hear it? He said: Yes."
"194","205 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Al-Layth informed me, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Hilal, from Nu'aym al-Mujmir, he said: I prayed behind Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, and he recited ""In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,"" then he recited the Mother of the Qur'an until he reached ""nor of those who went astray,"" then he said: Amin, and the people said: Amin, and he would say ""Allah is Greatest"" every time he prostrated, and when he rose from sitting he said: Allah is Greatest, and when he gave the salutation he said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I am indeed the one among you whose prayer most resembles the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"195","206 - Ibn al-Muqri', and Mahmud ibn Adam, and Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us - and this is the wording of Ibn al-Muqri' - he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi', from Ubadah ibn al-Samit as a marfu' narration, and he once said to me: that he reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer for one who does not recite the Opening of the Book (al-Fatihah)."
"196","207 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning al-Qattan - narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Maymun, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer except with the Opening of the Qur'an (al-Fatihah), and whatever is added to it. Abu Muhammad said: This Ja'far was one from whom al-Thawri and Isa ibn Yunus narrated."
"197","208 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, from Hammam, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the Dhuhr prayer, in the first two rak'ahs, the Opening of the Book and a surah in each rak'ah, and he would sometimes let us hear a verse, and he would lengthen the first rak'ah more than he lengthened the second, and he would recite in the last two rak'ahs the Opening of the Book in each rak'ah. He said: And likewise in the Asr prayer. He said: And likewise in the Fajr prayer."
"198","209 - Abu Muhammad said: And Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated it, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, with this chain, in the same manner, except that he did not mention: and the Fajr prayer. Muhammad ibn Idris narrated it to us, from al-Humaydi, from him."
"199","210 - Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, from Ata', he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, say: In every prayer there is recitation; whatever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made audible to us, we make audible to you, and whatever he kept hidden from us, we keep hidden from you, and I heard him say: There is no prayer except with recitation."
"200","211 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Ibrahim al-Saksaki, from Ibn Abi Awfa, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something that will suffice me instead of the Qur'an, so he said: Say: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no deity but Allah, and Allah is Greatest. 212 - Sufyan said: Yazid Abu Khalid al-Wasiti added: The man said: This is for my Lord, so what is for me? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, and grant me well-being. The man said: Four are for my Lord and four are for me."
"201","213 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Ibn Uyaynah informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the reciter says Amin, then say Amin, for the angels say Amin, so whoever's saying Amin coincides with the angels' saying Amin, his previous sins will be forgiven."
"202","214 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to say the takbir every time he lowered and raised himself, and he would say: I am indeed the one among you whose prayer most resembles the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"203","215 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim informed me, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata', he said: I heard Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi among ten of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one of whom was Abu Qatadah, may Allah be pleased with them, say: I am indeed the most knowledgeable among you of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: Why? For by Allah, you were neither the most frequent among us in following him nor the earliest among us in companionship with him. He said: Yes indeed. They said: Then demonstrate. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for prayer, he would raise his hands until he brought them level with his shoulders, then he would say the takbir until every bone settled in its place upright, then he would recite, then he would say the takbir and raise his hands until he brought them level with his shoulders, until every bone returned to its joint, then he would bow and place his palms on his knees, then he would straighten himself without lowering his head too much nor raising it, then he would raise his head and say: Allah hears him who praises Him, raising his hands until he brought them level with his shoulders upright. Abu Asim said: I think he said: Until every bone returned to its place. Then he would say: Allah is Greatest, then he would go down to the ground keeping his arms away from his sides, then he would prostrate, then he would raise his head and fold his left leg and sit upon it, and he would keep the toes of his feet open when he prostrated, then he would return and prostrate again, then he would raise his head and say: Allah is Greatest, and fold his left leg and sit upon it upright until every bone returned to its place, then he would do in the other rak'ah the same as that, until when he rose from the two rak'ahs he would say the takbir and raise his hands until he brought them level with his shoulders, as he did at the opening of the prayer, then he would do in the remainder of his prayer the same as that."
"204","216 - Muhammad narrated to us, he said: And Abu Asim narrated it to us another time, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata' narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi among ten of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one of whom was Abu Qatadah, say: I am indeed the most knowledgeable among you of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ibn Yahya said: And he transmitted the hadith in full."
"205","217 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Yahya ibn Khallad narrated to me, from his father, from his uncle Rifa'ah ibn Rafi', that he was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came and entered the mosque and prayed, then when he finished his prayer he came and greeted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the people, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: And upon you. Go back and pray, for you have not prayed. He said: So he went back and prayed. He said: So we began to watch his prayer, not knowing what fault he found in it, then when he finished his prayer he came and greeted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And upon you, go back and pray, for you have not prayed, and he mentioned that either twice or three times. Then the man said: I do not know what fault you found in my prayer, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of any one of you is not complete until he performs ablution thoroughly as Allah the Exalted commanded him, so he washes his face and his hands up to the elbows, and wipes his head and his feet up to the ankles, then he magnifies Allah and praises Him and glorifies Him, and recites from the Qur'an what Allah has permitted him therein and made easy, then he says the takbir and bows, placing his palms on his knees until his joints settle and relax, then he says: Allah hears him who praises Him, standing upright until every bone takes its position and he straightens his back, then he says the takbir and prostrates, placing his forehead firmly. Hammam said: And perhaps he said: Placing his face firmly on the ground, until his joints settle and relax, then he says the takbir and raises his head and sits upright until every bone returns to its place and he straightens his back, then he says the takbir and prostrates until his joints settle and relax, then he raises his head and says the takbir. When he does that, his prayer is complete."
"206","218 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah al-Darir, and Muhammad ibn Fudayl, and Ali ibn Ubayd, and Muhammad ibn Rabi'ah, and Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in which a man does not straighten his back in bowing and prostration does not suffice."
"207","219 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Abdullah - meaning Ibn Idris - informed me, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from Alqamah, he said: Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the prayer, so he said the takbir and raised his hands, then when he intended to bow he joined his hands together between his knees. He said: That reached Sa'd, so he said: My brother spoke the truth; we used to do this, then we were commanded with this - meaning: holding the knees - and he placed his hands on his knees."
"208","220 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us (h). And Ibn al-Muqri', and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head from the last rak'ah of the dawn prayer, he said: O Allah, save al-Walid ibn al-Walid, and Salamah ibn Hisham, and Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah, and the oppressed in Makkah. O Allah, make Your grip severe upon Mudar, and make it years upon them like the years of Yusuf."
"209","221 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nu'man Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Sadusi - whose nickname was Arim - narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn Yazid Abu Zayd al-Ahwal narrated to us, he said: Hilal narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a consecutive month in Dhuhr and Asr and Maghrib and Isha and Fajr, at the end of every prayer, when he said: Allah hears him who praises Him, in the last rak'ah, supplicating against a clan of Banu Sulaym, against Ri'l and Dhakwan, while those behind him said Amin. He said: He sent calling them to Islam, then they killed them. Ikrimah said: This is the key to the qunut."
"210","222 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to prostrate on seven - and he forbade tucking up hair or garments -: his hands and his knees and his forehead and the tips of his toes."
"211","223 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: By the One Who honored him and sent down the Book upon him, I indeed saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leading us in the Maghrib prayer one night while his forehead and the tip of his nose were indeed in water and mud."
"212","224 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you prostrates, let him place his hands, and when he rises, let him raise them, for the hands prostrate just as the face prostrates."
"213","225 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Abdullah - meaning Ibn Idris - narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, he said: I said: I shall certainly observe the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: When he opened the prayer he said the takbir and raised his hands, and I saw his thumbs close to his ears, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then he prostrated and placed his head between his hands at the same distance as when he opened the prayer."
"214","226 - Ibn al-Muqri', and Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Suhaym, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Ma'bad, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lifted the curtain while the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him - Ibn al-Muqri' said: And he once said: He intended to step back, so he signaled to him to remain, so he remained - then he said: O people, nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophethood except the righteous dream which a man sees or which is seen for him, then he said: Indeed I have been forbidden to recite while bowing or prostrating; as for bowing, then magnify the Lord in it, and as for prostration, then strive in supplication, for it is likely to be answered for you. Ibn al-Muqri' said: And he once said: ""So perhaps."" The hadith is that of Ibn al-Muqri'."
"215","227 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, he said: He came to us in our mosque and led us in prayer, then he said: I want to show you how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray. He said: When he raised his head from the second prostration, he would sit and lean upon the ground, then stand."
"216","228 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When we prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we used to say: Peace be upon Jibril, peace be upon Mika'il, peace be upon Israfil, peace be upon so-and-so and so-and-so, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to us and said: Indeed Allah is al-Salam, so when you sit in prayer, say: All greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and all good things; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; for when you say it, it reaches every righteous servant in the heaven and the earth: I bear witness that there is no deity but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, then let him choose whatever he wishes."
"217","229 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: Al-Hakam narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, he said: Ka'b ibn Ujrah met me and said: Shall I not present you with a gift, or shall I not relate to you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, we have known - or we have learned - the salutation upon you, so how should the invocation of blessings be? He said: Say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon the family of Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. And bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed the family of Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"218","230 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa - meaning Ibn Yunus - narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Muhammad ibn Abi A'ishah, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you performs the tashahhud, let him seek refuge from four: from the punishment of Hell, and the punishment of the grave, and the trial of life and death, and from the evil of the False Messiah, the Dajjal, then let him supplicate for himself with whatever occurs to him."
"219","231 - Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn Mahdi - narrated to us, from Za'idah ibn Qudamah, from Asim ibn Kulayb, he said: My father informed me that Wa'il ibn Hujr informed him, he said: I said: I shall certainly observe how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prays. He said: So I looked at him; he stood and said the takbir and raised his hands until they were level with his ears, then he placed his right palm on the back of his left palm and wrist and forearm, then he bowed and raised his hands the same as that, then he prostrated and placed his palms level with his ears, then he sat and spread his left leg and placed his left palm on his left thigh and left knee, and placed the edge of his right elbow on his right thigh, then he clasped two of his fingers and made a circle, then he raised his finger, and I saw him moving it in supplication. Then I came after that during a time in which there was cold, and I saw the people with most of their garments upon them moving their hands beneath their garments."
"220","232 - Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn Mahdi - informed me, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salutation to his right: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, and to his left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen from here, and the whiteness of his cheek from here."
"221","233 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Saying Subhan Allah is for men, and clapping is for women."
"222","234 - Ibn al-Muqri', and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, he heard Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with you that when something happens to you in your prayer you clap; this is only for women. Whoever is faced with something in his prayer, let him say: Subhan Allah."
"223","235 - Muhammad ibn Sa'id Abu Yahya al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Ulayyah narrated to us (h). And Ali ibn Khashram informed us that Ismail ibn Ulayyah informed them, from al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Mu'awiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami, he said: While we were praying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man from the people sneezed, so I said: May Allah have mercy on you, so the people stared at me, so I said: Woe to my mother, what is the matter with you that you look at me, so they began striking their hands upon their thighs, then when I saw them silencing me, I fell silent. Then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished - may my father and mother be sacrificed for him - by Allah, I never saw a teacher before him nor after him better in teaching than him; by Allah, he neither scolded me, nor insulted me, nor struck me. He said: This prayer of ours, nothing of this speech of people is proper in it; it is only glorification and magnification and recitation of the Qur'an, or as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am newly come from ignorance, and Allah has brought Islam, and among us are people who go to soothsayers. He said: Then do not go to them. I said: And among us are people who take omens. He said: That is something they find in their breasts, so let it not turn them away. He said: I said: And among us are people who draw lines. He said: A prophet used to draw lines, so whoever agrees with his line, then that is it. He said: And I had a slave girl who pastured sheep of mine in the direction of Uhud and al-Jawwaniyyah, then one day I looked at her and found that the wolf had taken a sheep from her sheep, and I am a man who feels regret as they feel regret, but I slapped her a slap, then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he deemed that grave against me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not free her? He said: Bring her to me. So I brought her to him, and he said to her: Where is Allah? She said: In the heaven. He said: Who am I? She said: You are the Messenger of Allah. He said: Free her, for she is a believer."
"224","236 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Damdam ibn Jaws, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the killing of the two black ones in prayer."
"225","237 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Maqburi, from Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Qatadah, may Allah be pleased with him: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed while Umamah bint Abi al-As was upon his neck; when he bowed he put her down, and when he stood he carried her."
"226","238 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Nafi' narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Quba to pray therein. He said: Then the Ansar came and greeted him while he was praying. He said: So I said: O Bilal, how did you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) respond to them when they greeted him while he was praying? He said: He says like this, and he spread his palm."
"227","239 - Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Layth, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Nabil, the Companion of al-Aba', from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Suhayb, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, so I greeted him, and he responded to me with a gesture. He said: I do not know except that he said: A gesture with his finger. 240 - And Ibn Uyaynah said: From Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, from Suhayb, may Allah be pleased with them."
"228","241 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Shu'ayb ibn al-Layth informed them, from al-Layth, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, so we prayed behind him while he was sitting, then he turned to us and saw us standing, so he signaled to us and we sat."
"229","242 - Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, he said: Mu'ayqib narrated to me, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about wiping in the mosque, he said: If you must do it, then once."
"230","243 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you stands for prayer, let him not wipe the pebbles, for mercy faces him."
"231","244 - Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-ikhtisar in prayer."
"232","245 - Hasan ibn Bishr ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you yawns in prayer, let him suppress it as much as he can, and if it overcomes him, let him place his hand upon his mouth."
"233","246 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Al-Fadl - meaning Ibn Musa - narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you passes wind in prayer, let him leave and hold his nose."
"234","247 - Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Ibn Wahb, from Amr ibn al-Harith, and Yunus ibn Yazid, and Ibn Sam'an, that Ibn Shihab informed them, he said: Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When supper is brought and the prayer comes, then begin with it before you pray the Maghrib prayer."
"235","248 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Uqbah narrated to me, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the Hajj, and he would pray two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, until he returned to Madinah. He said: I said: How long did you remain in Makkah? He said: Ten days."
"236","249 - Ibn al-Muqri', and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he heard Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz asking his companions: What have you heard about staying in Makkah? Al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid said: Al-Ala' ibn al-Hadrami informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The stay of the emigrant in Makkah after completing his rites is three days."
"237","250 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That when traveling pressed him, he would combine Maghrib and Isha."
"238","251 - Al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban narrated to me, he said: Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the voluntary prayer upon the back of his mount wherever it turned with him, then when he intended to pray the obligatory prayer, he would descend and face the qiblah."
"239","252 - Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Salim narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying while upon his mount, the supererogatory prayers in every direction, but he would lower the two prostrations below the bowing, gesturing with gestures."
"240","253 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell from a horse and his right side was scraped, so we entered upon him to visit him, then the prayer came and he prayed sitting, so we prayed sitting. Then when he finished his prayer, he said: The imam has only been appointed to be followed, so when he says the takbir, then say the takbir, and when he bows, then bow, and when he rises, then rise, and when he says: Allah hears him who praises Him - then say: Our Lord, and to You belongs praise, and when he prays sitting, then pray all sitting."
"241","254 - Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, he said: Husayn al-Mukattib narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the prayer of one sitting. He said: Whoever prays standing, it is better, and whoever prays sitting, he has half the reward of the standing one, and whoever prays lying down, he has half the reward of the sitting one."
"242","255 - And thus Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated it to us, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Husayn."
"243","256 - Hasan ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I had hemorrhoids, so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about prayer, so he said: Pray standing, and if you cannot, then sitting, and if you cannot, then upon your side."
"244","257 - Muhammad ibn Yahya, and Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Abu Ayyash al-Zuraqi, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Usfan. He said: The polytheists faced us, and Khalid ibn al-Walid was over them, and they were between us and the qiblah. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Dhuhr prayer, and they said: They were in a state in which had we attacked their unawares... Then they said: There is now coming upon them a prayer which is dearer to them than their children and their own selves. He said: So Jibril descended with this verse between Dhuhr and Asr: ""And when you are among them and lead them in prayer."" He said: So the prayer came, and he commanded them - Ibn Yahya said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and they said: So they took up arms, and we lined up behind him in two rows. He said: Then he bowed and we all bowed, then he rose and we all rose, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated with the row next to him, while the others stood guarding them. Then when they prostrated and stood, the others sat and prostrated in their place, then these advanced to the positions of those, and those came to the positions of these. He said: Then he bowed and they all bowed, then he rose and they all rose, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated along with the row next to him, while the others stood guarding them. He said: Then when they sat, the others sat and prostrated, then he gave salutation to them, then he left. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed it twice: once at Usfan, and once in the land of Banu Sulaym. 258 - And in a similar manner Ata', and Abu al-Zubayr narrated, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him."
"245","259 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the fear prayer with one group one rak'ah, while the other group faced the enemy. Then they left and stood in the position of their companions facing the enemy, and those others came and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them one rak'ah, then the Prophet gave salutation, then these made up one rak'ah, and those one rak'ah."
"246","260 - Abu Abdullah Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Anbasah al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', that Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, when asked about the fear prayer, would say: The imam advances with a group of the people, and the imam prays with them one rak'ah, while a group of them remain between him and the enemy who have not prayed. Then when those with him have prayed one rak'ah, they step back to the place of those who have not prayed, without giving salutation, and those who have not prayed advance and pray with him one rak'ah, then the imam leaves, having prayed two rak'ahs. Then each one of the two groups stands and prays for himself one rak'ah after the imam leaves, so each of the two groups will have prayed two rak'ahs. And if the fear is more intense than that, they pray on foot, standing upon their feet, or mounted, facing the qiblah or not facing it. Malik said: Nafi' said: I do not think Ibn Umar narrated it except from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"247","261 - Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Ibn Wahb, from Malik, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Salih ibn Khawwat, from one who prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Dhat al-Riqa' the fear prayer, that one group lined up with him, and one group lined up facing the enemy. So he prayed with those with him one rak'ah, then he remained standing while they completed for themselves, then they left and lined up facing the enemy, and the other group came and he prayed with them the remaining rak'ah of his prayer, then he remained sitting until they completed for themselves, then he gave salutation."
"248","262 - Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Salim narrated to me, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah said: Shu'bah, and Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Salih ibn Khawwat, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, that he said concerning the fear prayer: One group stands before the imam, and one group behind him, so he prays with those behind him one rak'ah and two prostrations, then he remains in his place until they make up one rak'ah and two prostrations, then they move to the position of their companions, then their companions move to the place of these, so he prays with them one rak'ah and two prostrations, then he remains in his place until they pray one rak'ah and two prostrations, then he gives salutation."
"249","263 - Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Salih ibn Khawwat, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the same as it."
"250","264 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Ya'la informed me, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: ""Whether you suffer harm from rain or you are ill"" - Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, was wounded."
"251","265 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sleeps past a prayer or forgets it, its expiation is to pray it when he remembers it."
"252","266 - Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Bashir Abu Ismail, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We halted for rest with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we did not wake until the sun hurt us. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let each man take hold of his mount's head, then move away from this place. Then he called for water and performed ablution, then he prostrated two prostrations, then the prayer was established and he prayed."
"253","267 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Al-Majishun Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah informed me, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you doubts while praying, whether in three or four, let him stand and pray one rak'ah, until the doubt is in the addition, then let him prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness before giving salutation. Then if he prayed five, they intercede for him, and if he prayed four, they enrage Satan."
"254","268 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi, and Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us, they said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed me, he said: Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj informed me that he heard Ibn Buhaynah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in prayer and stood up in the two rak'ahs, so we glorified Allah for him but he continued in his prayer, then he prostrated two prostrations, then gave salutation. The hadith is that of al-Darimi."
"255","269 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah ibn Abi Imran al-Hilali narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in one of the two afternoon prayers, either Dhuhr or Asr - I think it was Asr - so he prayed two rak'ahs then gave salutation, then he advanced and sat by a palm trunk as if angry. Then the hasty people went off saying: The prayer has been shortened, the prayer has been shortened. Then Dhu al-Yadayn advanced and said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened, or did you forget? So he said: Is Dhu al-Yadayn truthful? They said: Yes. He said: So he prayed two rak'ahs then gave salutation, and said the takbir and prostrated, then said the takbir and raised, then said the takbir and prostrated, then said the takbir and raised."
"256","270 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Za'idah ibn Qudamah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer and added in the prayer or decreased - Mansur said: Ibrahim said: The one who forgot that is Alqamah, or Alqamah from Abdullah - then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he turned to us with his face, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, has something new happened in the prayer? He said: And what is that? So we informed him of what he had done, then he folded his leg and faced the qiblah and prostrated two prostrations, then he turned to us and said: Had something new happened in the prayer I would have informed you, but I am a human who remembers as you remember, and forgets as you forget. So when I forget, remind me, and whichever of you doubts in his prayer, let him seek the closest of that to the correct and complete upon it, then give salutation, and prostrate two prostrations."
"257","271 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Asr prayer three rak'ahs and gave salutation, so he was told, then he prayed one rak'ah, then gave salutation, then he prostrated two prostrations, then gave salutation."
"258","272 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah, from Ibrahim, he said: Alqamah led them in prayer five rak'ahs. He said: So they said: O Abu Shibl, you added in the prayer. He said: So he said: I did not do so. He said: They said: Yes indeed. He said: Ibrahim said: So I said: Yes, from the side of the mosque. He said: So he said: And you, O one-eyed one, do you say that? He said: So he turned and prostrated with them two prostrations, then he related to them from Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in prayer five rak'ahs. He said: So he prostrated with them two prostrations, while sitting, and said: I am only a human who forgets as you forget. This Ibrahim is Ibn Suwayd al-Nakha'i, and he is not Ibrahim ibn Yazid al-Nakha'i."
"259","273 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath informed me, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in prayer and forgot in his prayer, so he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then he recited the tashahhud, then gave salutation."
"260","274 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif narrated to us, and I read it to Ibn Nafi', from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah and the people with him prayed. So he stood a long standing, about the length of Surah al-Baqarah, then he bowed a long bowing, then he rose and stood a long standing, shorter than the first standing, then he bowed a long bowing, shorter than the first bowing, then he prostrated. Ibn Yahya said: Perhaps they both said: Then he rose, or they did not say it. So he stood a long standing, shorter than the first standing, then he bowed a long bowing, shorter than the first bowing, then he rose and stood a long standing, shorter than the first standing, then he bowed a long bowing, shorter than the first bowing, then he prostrated, then he finished, and the sun had cleared. So he said: The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life, so when you see that, then remember Allah. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you take something in this station of yours, then we saw you draw back. So he said: I saw Paradise - or I was shown Paradise - so I took a bunch of grapes from it, and had I taken it, you would have eaten from it as long as the world remained. And I saw the Fire, and I never saw a sight like today at all, and I saw that most of its people were women. They said: Why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Due to their ingratitude. It was said: Do they disbelieve in Allah? He said: They are ungrateful to their husbands, and ungrateful for kindness; had you done good to one of them for the whole lifetime, then she saw something from you, she would say: I never saw any good from you at all."
"261","275 - Al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed me that al-Shafi'i informed them, he said: And I am Malik with this hadith, and he did not say in the place in which Muhammad ibn Yahya doubted: Then he rose."
"262","276 - Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Ibn Wahb, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The sun eclipsed in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the mosque and stood, and said the takbir, and the people lined up behind him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited a long recitation, then said the takbir and bowed a long bowing, then he raised his head and said: Allah hears him who praises Him; our Lord, and to You belongs praise. Then he stood and recited a long recitation, shorter than the first recitation, then said the takbir and bowed a long bowing, shorter than the first bowing, then he said: Allah hears him who praises Him; our Lord, and to You belongs praise. Then he did in the other rak'ah the same as that, completing four bowings and four prostrations, and the sun cleared before he finished. Then he stood and addressed the people, and praised Allah with what He deserves, then he said: The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they do not eclipse for the death of anyone or for his life, so when you see them, then hasten to prayer."
"263","277 - Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and prayed, prolonging the standing greatly, then he bowed and prolonged the bowing greatly, then he rose and prolonged the standing, shorter than the first standing, then he bowed, shorter than the first bowing, then he prostrated, then he stood and prolonged the standing, shorter than the first standing, then he bowed, shorter than the first bowing, then he raised his head and stood, shorter than the first standing, then he bowed, shorter than the first bowing, then he prostrated and finished his prayer, and the sun had cleared. Then he stood and addressed the people, praising Allah and extolling Him, then he said: The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they do not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life, so when you see that, then pray, and give charity, and remember Allah. Then he said: O nation of Muhammad, by Allah, there is no one more jealous than Allah that His servant commits adultery or His maidservant commits adultery. O nation of Muhammad, had you known what I know, you would have wept much and laughed little."
"264","278 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Tarkhan narrated to us, he said: Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir, from Asma' bint Abi Bakr, may Allah be pleased with her: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded freeing slaves during the solar eclipse."
"265","279 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, from Uththam ibn Ali, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Fatimah, from Asma', she said: We used to be commanded to free slaves during the solar eclipse."
"266","280 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Amr al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Kinanah, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out for seeking rain and did not deliver a sermon like these sermons of yours; he went out humble and unadorned, and prayed two rak'ahs as he prays the Eid."
"267","281 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the prayer ground and sought rain, so he faced the qiblah, and turned his cloak inside out, and prayed two rak'ahs."
"268","282 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out with the people seeking rain, so he prayed with them two rak'ahs, and recited aloud, and turned his cloak, and raised his hands, and supplicated, and sought rain, and faced the qiblah."
"269","283 - Abbas ibn al-Walid ibn Mazyad narrated to us that his father informed him, he said: I heard al-Awza'i, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, he said: The people were afflicted with drought in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon the pulpit addressing the people on a Friday, a Bedouin stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, wealth has perished, and families have hungered, so supplicate Allah for us. He said: So he raised his hands, while there was not a wisp of cloud in the sky. Then by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, he did not put them down until clouds like mountains gathered, then he did not descend from the pulpit until I saw the rain pouring down upon his beard. So we were rained upon that day of ours, and the next day, and the day after the next, and the one following it, until the next Friday. Then that Bedouin stood - or he said: A man other than him - and said: O Messenger of Allah, buildings have collapsed, so supplicate Allah for us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands and said: O Allah, around us, and not upon us. He said: He did not point with his hand to any direction of the mosque except that it parted, until it became like a hollow, and the valley - the valley of Qanat - flowed for a month, and no man came from any of the directions except that he reported abundance of rain."
"270","284 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus informed me, from Hisham, from Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah al-Ansariyyah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to bring them out on the day of Fitr and Nahr: the unmarried young women, and the menstruating women, and those secluded in chambers. As for the menstruating women, they keep away from the prayer place, and witness the good and the supplication of the Muslims. I said: O Messenger of Allah, one of them may not have a cloak? He said: Let her sister clothe her from her cloak."
"271","285 - Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn Mahdi - informed me, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a day of Fitr or Adha, so he prayed then addressed, then he came to the women and admonished them, and reminded them, and commanded them with charity."
"272","286 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed me, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata', from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a day of Eid, Fitr or Adha, so he began with the prayer before the sermon, without adhan and without iqamah."
"273","287 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: That a spear would be planted for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would pray toward it on the day of Eid."
"274","288 - And Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated it to us another time, and he did not mention: On the day of Eid."
"275","289 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Adi - meaning Ibn Thabit - from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on the day of Fitr and prayed two rak'ahs, praying neither before them nor after them."
"276","290 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Abdullah - meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'la al-Ta'ifi - narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the takbir in the Eid, on the day of Fitr, seven times in the first, and five times in the last, apart from the takbir of prayer."
"277","291 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said: Hasan ibn Muslim informed me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I witnessed the Fitr prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them, and all of them prayed it before the sermon, then addressed after. He said: Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended as if I am looking at him when he seated the men with his hand, then he came cutting through them until he came to the women, with Bilal with him. So he said: ""O Prophet, when the believing women come to you pledging to you that they will not associate anything with Allah."" So he recited this verse until he finished from it, then he said when he finished from it: Are you upon that? Then one woman said - none other than her among them answered: Yes, O Prophet of Allah - Hasan does not know who she is - He said: So give charity. He said: So Bilal spread his garment, then he said: Come on, for you, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. So they began casting rings and signet rings into the garment of Bilal."
"278","292 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Al-Fadl - meaning Ibn Musa - narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, from Ata', from Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib, he said: I attended the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a day of Eid, so he said: You have completed the prayer, so whoever of you wishes, let him sit for the sermon, and whoever wishes to go, let him go."
"279","293 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from his father, from Habib ibn Salim, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them both: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the Eid: ""Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High"" and ""Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming."" Then when Eid and Friday coincided, he recited them both in both."
"280","294 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Bishr informed me, from Abu Umayr ibn Anas, my paternal uncles among the Ansar, among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed me, they said: The crescent of Shawwal was obscured from us, so we woke fasting. Then riders came at the end of the day and testified before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that they had seen the crescent the day before. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to break fast from their day, and to go out for their Eid the next morning."
"281","295 - Ibn al-Muqri' and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night prayer is two by two, so when you fear the dawn, then pray witr with one rak'ah. Mahmud added: It makes odd for you what has passed."
"282","296 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ya'fur, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr at every part of the night, and his witr ended at the predawn."
"283","297 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you fears not waking at the end of the night, let him pray witr at its beginning and sleep, and whoever among you hopes to wake at the end of the night, let him pray witr at its end, for the prayer at the end of the night is witnessed, so that is better."
"284","298 - Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Ibn Wahb, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to glorify Allah upon the mount facing whichever direction it turned, and pray witr upon it, except that he would not pray upon it the obligatory prayer."
"285","299 - Ibrahim ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah Abu Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Talhah al-Yami, from Dharr, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the witr: ""Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High"" and ""Say: O disbelievers"" and ""Say: He is Allah, the One."" Then when he gave salutation, he would say: Glory be to the Sovereign, the Most Holy, glory be to the Sovereign, the Most Holy, three times."
"286","300 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra', from al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me words to say in the qunut of witr: O Allah, guide me among those You have guided, and grant me well-being among those You have granted well-being, and befriend me among those You have befriended, and bless for me in what You have given, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed, for indeed You decree and none decrees upon You, and indeed he whom You befriend is not humiliated. Blessed are You, our Lord, and Exalted."
"287","301 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra', from al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught him these words to say in the qunut of witr."
"288","302 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to me, he said: Nafi' narrated to me that Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to say: Whoever prays at night, let him make the last of his prayer witr, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that. When dawn comes, the night prayer and the witr have gone, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray witr before dawn."
"289","Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Nafi' informed me that Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say: whoever prays at night should make the last of his prayer witr before dawn; that is how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command them. Ibn Yahya said: Hajjaj would bring the two reports together in one continuous chain."
"290","Chapter on the sunnah rak'ahs. Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two rak'ahs before Zuhr and two after it, two after Maghrib in his house, and two after 'Isha in his house. And Hafsah told me - and hers was an hour when no one entered upon him - that he used to pray two rak'ahs when dawn broke and the caller announced the prayer - Ayyub said: I think they were light ones - and two rak'ahs after Friday prayer in his house."
"291","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim and Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, they said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid informed us, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I asked 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) about the voluntary prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: he used to pray four before Zuhr in my house, then go out and lead the people in prayer, then return to my house and pray two rak'ahs."
"292","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata, from 'Ali ibn 'Abdullah al-Bariqi, from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night and day prayers are two by two."
"293","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: and from what I read to Ibn Nafi', and Mutarrif narrated to me, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray eleven rak'ahs at night, making the witr one of them; when he finished he would lie down on his right side until the caller came to him, then he would pray two light rak'ahs."
"294","Chapter on the times when prayer is forbidden. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: none of you should seek out the rising of the sun or its setting [to pray then]; for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid that."
"295","Muhammad narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Wahb ibn al-Ajda', from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade praying after 'Asr unless the sun is still high."
"296","Chapter on Friday. Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is an hour on Friday that no man meets while praying and asking Allah for good but He gives it to him."
"297","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever of you comes to Friday prayer should bathe."
"298","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from 'Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), in a report raised to the Prophet: Bathing on Friday is obligatory upon every adult."
"299","'Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn Mahdi - narrated to us, from Hammam, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution on Friday prayer, it suffices him and is good; and whoever bathes, bathing is better."
"300","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: At every door of the mosque there are angels writing the people, the first then the first; when the imam sits down they fold the scrolls and listen to the sermon. The early comer is like one offering a camel, then the one after him like one offering a cow, then the one after him like one offering a ram, until he mentioned the chicken and the egg."
"301","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Khalid ibn Mawhab narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Faddalah narrated to us, from 'Ayyash ibn 'Abbas, from Bukayr ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), from Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with her), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Upon every adult is going early to Friday prayer, and upon whoever goes to Friday prayer is bathing."
"302","'Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, he said: 'Ubaydah ibn Sufyan narrated to me, from Abu al-Ja'd 'Amr ibn Bakr al-Damri, who was a Companion, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever abandons three Friday prayers out of neglect, his heart is sealed."
"303","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Abu Dawud, from Fulayh, from 'Uthman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Taymi, he heard Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) say: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lead us in Friday prayer when the sun had passed its zenith."
"304","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Amir 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Amr al-'Aqadi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, he said: the call on Friday - when the imam came out and when the prayer was established - in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) was one; then in the time of 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) houses multiplied, so he ordered the third call at al-Zawra, and it remained until now."
"305","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, and Muhammad ibn Abi Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf narrated to me, that his father told him that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik said: I used to lead my father after he lost his sight, and whenever he heard the call on Friday he would say: may Allah have mercy on Abu Umamah. So I said to my father: I like your praying for Abu Umamah whenever you hear the call on Friday. He said: my son, he was the first to gather us for Friday prayer in Madinah, in Hazm al-Nabit in the Harrah of Banu Bayadah, in a meadow called Naqi' al-Khadabat. I said: how many were you that day? He said: forty men."
"306","Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Husayn, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: a caravan arrived while we were praying Friday prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the people dispersed, leaving only twelve men; then was revealed: (But when they saw trade or amusement, they dispersed to it)."
"307","Ibn al-Muqri and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: a man entered on Friday while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was preaching. He said: have you prayed? He said: no. He said: stand and pray two rak'ahs."
"308","Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: and I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrating from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from 'Abdullah ibn Busr, he said: I was sitting beside him on Friday when a man came stepping over people's necks on Friday while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was preaching, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: sit down, for you have annoyed [people] and come late. Abu al-Zahiriyyah said: and we would talk with him until the imam came out."
"309","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach two sermons on Friday, with a sitting between them."
"310","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach standing, then sit, then stand, reciting verses and remembering Allah; his sermon was moderate and his prayer was moderate."
"311","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Abd al-Majid al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preached, his eyes would redden, his voice would rise and his anger intensify, as if he were warning of an army, saying: may [the enemy] come upon you morning and evening. And he would say: I have been sent, I and the Hour, like these two, joining his index and middle fingers. And he would say: to proceed, the best speech is the Book of Allah, the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad, the worst of matters are newly invented ones, and every innovation is misguidance. Then he would say: I am closer to every believer than his own self; whoever leaves wealth, it is for his family, and whoever leaves debt or dependents, it is to me and upon me."
"312","Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman - meaning Ibn Bilal - narrated to me, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from his father, he said: I heard Jabir ibn 'Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) say: the sermon of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Friday was: praising Allah and extolling Him, then saying after that in a raised voice - and he mentioned something similar."
"313","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), raising it to the Prophet: If you say on Friday while the imam is preaching, be quiet, you have engaged in idle talk."
"314","Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: 'Uqbah narrated to me, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, he said: I heard my father narrating, from Habib ibn Salim, the freedman of al-Nu'man, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with them both): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Friday prayer (Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High) and (Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming)."
"315","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi': that Marwan ibn al-Hakam appointed Abu Hurayrah over Madinah, and Abu Hurayrah led them in Friday prayer, reciting Surah al-Jumu'ah in the first rak'ah and (When the hypocrites come to you) in the second. 'Ubaydullah said: when Abu Hurayrah finished, I walked beside him and said: you recited two surahs I heard 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reciting in Kufah. Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting them."
"316","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn 'Abd Rabbihi narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: al-Mughirah al-Dabbi narrated to me, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Two festivals have coincided on this day of yours; whoever of you wishes, it suffices him instead of Friday prayer, but we shall hold the congregation, Allah willing."
"317","Chapter on congregation and leadership in prayer. 'Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Malik, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The excellence of congregational prayer over a man's prayer alone is twenty-five parts."
"318","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had intended to order men to lead the prayer, then order my youths to go to people who do not attend it and burn their houses over them with bundles of firewood; if one of them knew he would find a fat bone or two good trotters, he would attend 'Isha."
"319","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you come to prayer, do not come rushing; come walking, calmly; whatever you catch, pray, and whatever you miss, complete."
"320","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established... similar, and he said: then complete it. And Shu'ayb, 'Uqayl, Ibn Abi Dhi'b and others said in this report: then complete it."
"321","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman al-'Ijli narrated to us, he said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both): that when the Emigrants came from Makkah to Madinah they stayed at al-'Usbah beside Quba, and Salim the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah led them in prayer because he knew the most Qur'an among them; among them were Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Asad and 'Umar."
"322","Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Isma'il ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Dam'aj, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people should be led by the one who recites the Book of Allah best; if they are equal in recitation, then the most knowledgeable of the Sunnah; if equal in the Sunnah, then the earliest in emigration; if equal in emigration, then the oldest. A man should not be led in prayer in his place of authority, nor should one sit on his honored seat in his house except with his permission."
"323","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, he said: 'Amr ibn Salamah Abu Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: we were at a watering place on the people's route, and we would ask them about this matter. He mentioned part of the report. He said: my father went with the acceptance of Islam of our clan. He stayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as long as Allah willed, then returned. When he drew near we met him, and when we saw him he said: I have come to you, by Allah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in truth. Then he said: he commands you such-and-such and forbids you such-and-such, and to pray such prayer at such time; when prayer comes, one of you should call the adhan and the one who knows most Qur'an should lead you. The people of our clan looked and found no one knowing more Qur'an than me, because of what I had memorized from the riders. So they put me forward and I led them though I was six years old."
"324","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to me, he said: 'Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Ibn Umm Maktum in charge of Madinah twice; and I saw him on the day of al-Qadisiyyah carrying a black banner."
"325","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim who heard Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi say: a dispute arose between two clans of the Ansar over a pre-Islamic matter until Satan sowed discord between them - once he said: until they attacked one another. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told, so he went to them and was delayed. Bilal called the adhan, and when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was late in coming, Bilal established the prayer and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) stepped forward. As he stepped forward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, with Abu Bakr leading the people, and he passed through the rows until he reached the first row. Abu Bakr would not turn in his prayer, so the people clapped with their hands. When he heard the clapping he turned and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) signaled to him to stay - once he said: he raised his head to the sky - but Abu Bakr stepped back, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward. When he finished his prayer he said: what prevented you, O Abu Bakr, from staying firm? He said: Allah would not let the son of Abu Quhafah be seen in front of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"326","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad - meaning Ibn Ja'far - informed me, he said: Abu Hazim informed me, he said: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) say: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once prayed on the pulpit with the people behind him, bowing, then rising and stepping back, prostrating on the ground, then returning and climbing it; whenever he prostrated he came down. When he finished he said: O people, I prayed before you like this as you see me so that you may follow me."
"327","Chapter on the imam praying on a raised bench. 'Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: 'Isa informed us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Hammam, he said: Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) prayed on a bench in Madinah with Abu Mas'ud behind him, who took his garment and pulled him. When he finished, Abu Mas'ud said to him: did you not know this is disliked? He said: yes, do you not see I remembered it."
"328","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to me, from his uncle Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I prayed with an orphan behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Umm Sulaym prayed behind us."
"329","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Umarah ibn 'Umayr, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abu Mas'ud 'Uqbah ibn 'Amr, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe our shoulders in prayer and say: be straight and do not differ, lest your hearts differ."
"330","'Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: Talhah ibn Musarrif narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awsajah, from al-Bara ibn 'Azib (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: he used to come to us when we stood for prayer and wipe our chests and shoulders, saying: let not your rows differ, lest your hearts differ. And he used to say: Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row - or he said: the foremost rows."
"331","'Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn 'Ajlan, he said: my father informed me, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: the best rows of men in prayer are the foremost, and the worst are the last; perhaps he said: and the worst rows of women in prayer are the foremost, and the best are the last. The doubt is from Abu Muhammad."
"332","Chapter on a man praying alone behind the congregation. 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from Ziyad al-A'lam, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him): that he bowed before reaching the row, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: may Allah increase you in eagerness, but do not repeat it."
"333","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: al-Thawri informed us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Wabisah: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying alone behind the congregation and ordered him to repeat the prayer."
"334","Chapter on silence between the takbir and the recitation. 'Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Muhammad - meaning Ibn Fudayl - informed us, from 'Umarah, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the takbir, he would pause between the takbir and the recitation. I said to him: may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, what do you say in your silence between the takbir and the recitation? He said: I say: O Allah, distance me from my sins as You distanced the east from the west; O Allah, purify me of my sins as the white garment is purified of dirt; O Allah, wash me of my sins with snow, water and hail."
"335","Chapter on recitation behind the imam. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Makhul, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi', from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the dawn prayer and the recitation became heavy for him; when he finished he said: I see you recite behind your imam. We said: yes, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, quickly. He said: do not do so except with the Mother of the Qur'an, for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it."
"336","Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Ibn Wahb, from Malik ibn Anas and Yunus ibn Yazid, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the imam says amin, say amin, for the angels say amin; whoever's amin coincides with the angels' amin, his past sins are forgiven."
"337","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever catches a rak'ah of the prayer has caught it."
"338","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan informed us, from Ibn 'Ajlan, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban narrated to us, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not precede me in bowing or prostration; whatever I precede you in when I bow, you will catch me in when I rise, and whatever I precede you in when I prostrate, you will catch me in when I rise; for I have grown heavy."
"339","Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does not one of you fear, when he raises his head while the imam is prostrating, that Allah will turn his head into a donkey's head or his form into a donkey's form."
"340","Chapter on lightening the prayer for the people. Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn Abi Hazim narrated to me, from Abu Mas'ud 'Uqbah ibn 'Amr, he said: a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I stay away from the dawn prayer because of so-and-so, who prolongs it for us. I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) angrier in admonition than on that day. He said: O people, some of you drive people away; so whichever of you leads people in prayer should be brief, for among them are the weak, the elderly, and those with needs."
"341","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) used to pray 'Isha with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then return and lead us. One night the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the prayer, and Mu'adh came and recited Surah al-Baqarah. When a man saw that, he stepped back and prayed, then left. When they finished they said: O so-and-so, have you turned hypocrite? He said: no, but I shall go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and tell him. So he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Mu'adh used to pray with you then return and lead us; you delayed the prayer last night, so he came and recited al-Baqarah; when I saw that I stepped aside and prayed, for we are owners of water-camels and workers with our hands. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: are you a source of trial? Recite such-and-such surah and such-and-such surah. Abu al-Zubayr said, from Jabir: Recite Surah Sabbih, Hal ataka, (By the night when it covers), and the like."
"342","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi 'A'ishah, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) to lead the people in prayer. She said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in front of Abu Bakr, seated, while Abu Bakr prayed behind him. Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that Abu Bakr was the foremost."
"343","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Isa narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, he said: observing prayer was mentioned in the presence of 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), and she said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being brought out, supported between two men with his feet dragging on the ground, until he was brought to Abu Bakr while he was leading the people in prayer; he was seated to the left of Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr prayed following the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the people prayed following the prayer of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"344","Abu Muhammad said: and thus Abu Mu'awiyah narrated it, from al-A'mash: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and sat to the left of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"345","And in the report of Abu Ishaq, from Arqam, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him): Abu Bakr followed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the people followed Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"346","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Aswad narrated to us, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying in the mosque and said: will no man make a profitable trade with this one and pray with him."
"347","'Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash informed us, from 'Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: you may live to meet people who pray the prayer outside its time; if you meet them, pray in your houses at the time you know, then pray with them and make it voluntary."
"348","'Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: 'Isa - meaning Ibn Yunus - informed us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah, and when they go out let them go out unattractive."
"349","Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn 'Abdullah ibn Jumay', from his grandmother, and from Ibn Khallad, from Umm Waraqah: that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to Badr, she said to him: O Messenger of Allah, let me go with you to nurse your sick and treat your wounded, that Allah may grant me martyrdom. He said: stay in your house, for Allah will grant you martyrdom. She used to be called the martyr; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would visit her on Fridays and say: let us go to the martyr. She had recited the Qur'an, and she asked permission for a caller to prayer to be appointed in her house so she might pray; he permitted her."
"350","The beginning of the Book of Zakat. Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Marwan - meaning Ibn Mu'awiyah - narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, from Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to establish prayer, give zakat, and give sincere advice to every Muslim."
"351","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn 'Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: there is no owner of camels who does not pay their due but they will come on the Day of Resurrection more numerous than ever, and he will be seated for them on a flat plain where they trample him with their hooves and feet; no owner of cattle who does not pay their due but they will come on the Day of Resurrection more numerous than ever, and he will be seated for them on a flat plain where they gore him with their horns and trample him with their hooves; no owner of sheep who does not pay their due but they will come on the Day of Resurrection more numerous than ever, and he will be seated for them on a flat plain where they butt him with their horns and trample him with their cloven hooves, none of them hornless or broken-horned; and no owner of treasure who does not pay its due but his treasure will come on the Day of Resurrection as a bald serpent following him with its mouth open; when it comes to him he flees from it, and it calls to him: take your treasure which you hoarded, for I have no need of it; when he sees there is no escape, he puts his hand in its mouth and it bites it with the bite of a stallion. Abu al-Zubayr said: and I heard 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr say this, then we asked Jabir ibn 'Abdullah about it and he said the same as 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr. Abu al-Zubayr said: and I heard 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr say: a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the due of camels? He said: milking them at the water, lending their bucket and their stallion, granting their milk, and carrying loads on them in the path of Allah."
"352","'Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah - meaning Ibn Wahb - informed us, from 'Amr ibn al-Harith, from Darraj Abu al-Samh, from Ibn Hujayrah al-Khawlani, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you have paid the zakat of your wealth, you have fulfilled what is upon you; and whoever gathers unlawful wealth and gives it in charity gets no reward for it, and its burden remains upon him."
"353","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Burayd ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Burdah narrated to me, from his grandfather Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and two men of my cousins; one of the two men said: O Messenger of Allah, appoint me over some of what Allah has entrusted to you, and the other said the same. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: we do not appoint to this office one who asks for it, nor one who is eager for it."
"354","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Uthman ibn 'Umar ibn Faris narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Awn informed us, from al-Hasan, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not ask for leadership; if you are given it without asking, you will be helped in it, and if you are given it after asking, you will be left to it."
"355","Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Shimasah, he said: I heard 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The collector of the toll tax - meaning the tithe-taker - shall not enter Paradise."
"356","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Yahya ibn 'Umarah ibn Abi Hasan al-Mazini, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - Ibn al-Muqri said: and once he said it as a report: There is no charity due on less than five uqiyyahs, no charity on less than five awsuq, and no charity on less than five dhawd."
"357","'Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - that is Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, he said: my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: For every forty grazing camels, a bint labun; camels shall not be separated from their count. Whoever gives it seeking reward gets its reward, and whoever withholds it, we shall take it and half his camels - a firm decree from the decrees of our Lord; none of it is lawful for the family of Muhammad."
"358","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna ibn 'Abdullah ibn Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Thumamah ibn 'Abdullah ibn Anas, that he heard Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) say: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq sent me to Bahrain and wrote for me this letter: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. This is the obligation of charity which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) imposed upon the Muslims, which Allah commanded His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with: whoever of the believers is asked for it in its proper amounts should give it, and whoever is asked for more should not give it. For twenty-four camels or fewer, sheep: one sheep for every five. When they reach twenty-five to thirty-five, a female bint makhad; if there is no female bint makhad, a male ibn labun. From thirty-six to forty-five, a bint labun. From forty-six to sixty, a hiqqah ready to be mounted by the stallion. From sixty-one to seventy-five, a jadha'ah. From seventy-six to ninety, two bint labuns. From ninety-one to one hundred twenty, two hiqqahs ready for the stallion. Beyond one hundred twenty, for every forty a bint labun and for every fifty a hiqqah. When ages of camels differ in charity obligations: one whose due reaches a jadha'ah but has no jadha'ah and has a hiqqah, the hiqqah is accepted from him with two sheep if available, or twenty dirhams. One whose due is a hiqqah but has no hiqqah and has a jadha'ah, the jadha'ah is accepted and the collector pays him twenty dirhams or two sheep. One whose due is a hiqqah but has only a bint labun, it is accepted with two sheep or twenty dirhams. One whose due is a bint labun but has a hiqqah, the hiqqah is accepted and the collector pays him twenty dirhams or two sheep. One whose due is a bint labun but has only a bint makhad, it is accepted and he pays twenty dirhams or two sheep. One whose due is a bint makhad but has a bint labun, it is accepted and the collector pays him twenty dirhams or two sheep. One who has no bint makhad as due but has a male ibn labun, the ibn labun is accepted with nothing extra. One who has only four camels owes nothing unless its owner wishes; at five camels, one sheep is due. For sheep charity on grazing sheep: at forty sheep, one sheep up to one hundred twenty; above one hundred twenty up to two hundred, two sheep; above two hundred up to three hundred, three sheep; above three hundred, one sheep per hundred. No old, defective, or male goat shall be taken in charity unless the collector wishes. Separated animals shall not be joined, nor joined ones separated, for fear of charity. Two partners settle evenly between them. If a man's grazing sheep are one short of forty, there is no charity unless its owner wishes. For silver, a quarter of a tenth; if one's wealth is only one hundred ninety dirhams, there is no charity unless its owner wishes."
"359","Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us. And Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us, he said: Qabisah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Masruq, from Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to Yemen and ordered him to take from cattle one musinnah for every forty and one tabi' or tabi'ah for every thirty. And Ahmad ibn Yusuf said: the Prophet sent him to Yemen and so ordered him."
"360","Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Salam - meaning Ibn Harb - narrated to us, he said: Khusayf informed us, from Abu 'Ubaydah, from 'Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For thirty cattle, a tabi' or tabi'ah, and for forty, a musinnah."
"361","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us as a preacher and said: Their charities shall not be taken except in their homes."
"362","Abu Hatim al-Razi Muhammad ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Salih ibn Muslim al-'Ijli narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from his uncle 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The charities of desert folk are taken at their waters and courtyards."
"363","Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Ibn Wahb, he said: 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Abu al-Zubayr narrated to him, that he heard Jabir ibn 'Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) mention that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For what rivers and springs irrigate, a tenth; for what is irrigated by the water-wheel, half a tenth."
"364","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim ibn 'Abdullah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he laid down: For what the sky and springs irrigate, or what is naturally watered, a tenth; for what is irrigated by drawing water, half a tenth."
"365","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Yahya ibn 'Umarah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity due on less than five awsuq of grain or dates."
"366","Bahr ibn Nasr informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Yahya ibn 'Abdullah ibn Salim informed me, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Banu Shababah - a clan of Fahm - used to pay to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a tenth from honey they had, one skin out of every ten skins, and he would protect two valleys for them; then they paid to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) what they used to pay to the Messenger of Allah, and he protected their two valleys."
"367","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, from 'Abbad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from 'Attab ibn Asid (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him and ordered him to estimate grapes as he estimates dates, and to take zakat of grapes as raisins as he takes zakat of dates as dates."
"368","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Khubayb, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mas'ud ibn Niyar, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you estimate, take and leave; leave a third, and if you do not leave a third, leave a quarter."
"369","Ishaq ibn 'Abdullah al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from 'Amr al-Thaqafi, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a large gold ring in his hand and said: do you pay zakat on this? He said: and what is its zakat? When he turned away, he said: a great ember. Abu Muhammad said: al-Walid ibn Muslim said in this regard, from Sufyan, from 'Umar ibn Ya'la al-Ta'ifi."
"370","'Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Uyaynah informed us, from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from 'Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no charity due upon a Muslim for his horse or his slave."
"371","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from 'Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no charity due upon a Muslim for his horse or his slave."
"372","Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Ibn Wahb, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar and Malik narrated to me, from Nafi', from 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made obligatory upon the people the zakat of fitr in Ramadan, a sa' of dates or a sa' of barley, upon every free person or slave, male or female, among the Muslims."
"373","'Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Qays, he said: 'Iyad narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id, he said: we continued to give charity in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a sa' of dates, raisins, dried curd, barley grain, or barley; we kept giving it until Mu'awiyah's time, when he said: I consider two mudds of Syrian wheat equal to a sa' of barley. So the people adopted it."
"374","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Qays informed us with this chain similarly, adding: Abu Sa'id said: as for me, I shall keep giving it as I used to give it, always."
"375","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Musa ibn 'Uqbah informed me, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the zakat of fitr before people go out to the prayer ground."
"376","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya al-Asadi narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Dinar, from al-Hakam ibn 'Utaybah, from Hujayyah ibn 'Adi, from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): that al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about paying his charity early before it was due, and he permitted him that. Yahya ibn Ma'in said: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya al-Khulqani is trustworthy, and al-Hajjaj ibn Dinar al-Wasiti is trustworthy."
"377","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed me, he said: 'Amr ibn Murrah informed me, he said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: when a household brought charity to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would pray for them; my father brought him charity, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, send blessings upon the family of Abu Awfa."
"378","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him): that he gave a horse in the path of Allah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave it to a man; the man kept it to sell it, so 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him: is the horse I gave in the path of Allah for sale? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: do not buy it, and do not take back your charity."
"379","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Rayhan ibn Yazid al-'Amiri, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is not lawful for a rich man, nor for one strong and able-bodied."
"380","Al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is not lawful for a rich man, nor for one strong and able-bodied."
"381","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from 'Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is not lawful for a rich man except for five: one employed to collect it, a man who bought it with his money, a debtor, a fighter in the path of Allah, or a poor person to whom charity was given from it and he gifted some of it to a rich man."
"382","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: and from what I read to 'Abdullah ibn Nafi', and Mutarrif narrated to me, from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from 'Ata ibn Yasar, from a man of Banu Asad, he said: I stayed with my family at Baqi' al-Gharqad, and my family said to me: go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him for something for us to eat, mentioning their need. So I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found a man asking him, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I find nothing to give you. The man turned away angry, saying: by my life, you give to whom you wish. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: he is angry with me for not finding what to give him; whoever of you asks while possessing an uqiyyah or its equivalent has asked importunately. The Asadi said: I said: our milch camel is better than an uqiyyah. Malik said: an uqiyyah is forty dirhams. So I returned without asking. Later barley and raisins came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he distributed some to us until Allah enriched us from His bounty."
"383","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Harun ibn Ri'ab, from Kinanah ibn Nu'aym, from Qabisah ibn Mukhariq, he said: I undertook a surety debt and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: we shall pay it for you, disbursing it when the charity camels arrive. He said: O Qabisah, begging is forbidden except in one of three cases: a man who undertook a surety debt, for whom begging is lawful until he pays it, then he refrains; a man struck by a calamity that destroyed his wealth, for whom begging is lawful, asking until he obtains enough to live on, then he refrains; and a man struck by need and poverty until three wise men of his people testify, for whom begging is lawful until he obtains enough to live on, then he refrains; anything besides that of begging is ill-gotten."
"384","Abu Hashim Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Isma'il - meaning Ibn 'Ulayyah - narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Awn narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) acquired land at Khaybar and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking his counsel about it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have acquired land at Khaybar, no wealth dearer to me; he said: if you wish, keep its principal and give it in charity. So 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave it in charity: its principal not to be sold, gifted, or inherited; he gave it for the poor, debtors, slaves, in the path of Allah, the traveler, and the guest. There is no sin upon whoever administers it to eat from it reasonably, or to feed a friend without amassing wealth from it."
"385","Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Ismail narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, similar to the hadith of Ibn Awn, and he said: A man of sound judgment from the family of Umar will take charge of it."
"386","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Jafar, informed us, he said: Al-Ala informed me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man dies, his deeds are cut off except from three: ongoing charity, knowledge that benefits, or a righteous child who prays for him."
"387","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Rabiah, from al-Harith ibn Bilal ibn al-Harith, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took zakat from the mines of al-Qabaliyyah."
"388","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: The first time I saw al-Zuhri I asked him about this hadith, and he narrated to me, he said: Said and Abu Salamah narrated to me that they heard Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The wound of a dumb animal is without liability, the mine is without liability, and on buried treasure is a fifth."
"389","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As (may Allah be pleased with him): that the delegation of Thaqif came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he lodged them in the mosque so their hearts would be softened. They stipulated with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that they would not be conscripted, nor tithed, nor made to bow, and that no one from outside them would be appointed over them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will not be conscripted, nor tithed, and no one other than you will be appointed over you, but there is no good in a religion in which there is no bowing."
"390","Muhammad ibn Yahya and al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, they said: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abu Jamrah informed me, he said: Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to seat me on his couch, he said: When the delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Who are the people, or who is the delegation? They said: From Rabiah. He said: Welcome to the delegation, or to the people, without disgrace or regret. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we cannot come to you except in the sacred month, and between us and you is this tribe of the disbelievers of Mudar, so inform us of a decisive matter which we may convey to those behind us and by which we may enter Paradise. He said: And they asked him about drinks. He said: He commanded them with four and forbade them from four. He said: He commanded them to believe in Allah alone. He said: Do you know what belief in Allah alone is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Testifying that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakat, fasting Ramadan, and giving a fifth of the spoils. And he forbade them from hantam, dubba, naqir, and perhaps he said muqayyar, and muzaffat. And he said: Memorize them and inform those behind you of them."
"391","Muhammad ibn Yahya and Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, that he heard Muhammad ibn Hunayn saying: Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to disapprove of fasting in advance of Ramadan when the crescent of the month of Ramadan had not been seen. He says: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you do not see the crescent, then complete thirty nights."
"392","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa, meaning Ibn Yunus, informed us, from Shubah, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, or he said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Shubah doubted: Fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it, and if it is obscured from you, then count thirty."
"393","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qays, he said: I was sent to Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) to ask her about fasting Ramadan when the crescent is hidden, and about prayer after Asr. So I entered upon Aishah and said: So-and-so sends you greetings of peace; he sent me to you to ask you about prayer after Asr, and about continuous fasting, and about fasting in the month of Ramadan. He mentioned part of the hadith. He said: She said: He used to take care to observe Shaban as he did not take care with any other month, then he would fast upon sighting Ramadan; if it was obscured for him he would count thirty, then fast, meaning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"394","Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Waki narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Mubarak, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not precede the month of Ramadan by fasting a day or two days, except a man who was fasting a regular fast, then let him fast it."
"395","Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Al-Fadl, meaning Ibn Musa, narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have seen the crescent. He said: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger? He said: Yes. He said: Then he called out to fast."
"396","Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Dhuhli narrated to us, from al-Husayn ibn Ali, from Zaidah, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have seen the crescent. He said: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. He said: O Bilal, announce among the people that they should fast tomorrow."
"397","Ibrahim ibn Marzuq informed us, he said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Concession was granted to the very old man and the very old woman in that, while they were able to fast, to break fast if they wished, or to feed a poor person for each day, with no makeup upon them. Then that was abrogated in this verse: So whoever witnesses the month, let him fast it. And it remained for the very old man and the very old woman if they cannot fast, and for the pregnant woman and the nursing woman, if they feared, they break fast and feed a poor person for each day."
"398","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Uthman, from Ibn Masud (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the adhan of Bilal prevent you from your sahur, for Bilal calls adhan to wake your sleeper, and it is not like this or like this until it is like this and like this, meaning the dawn."
"399","Said ibn Bahr al-Qaratis narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take sahur, for in sahur there is blessing."
"400","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am ruined. He said: What is the matter with you? He said: I had intercourse with my wife in Ramadan. He said: Can you free a slave? He said: No. He said: Can you fast two consecutive months? He said: No. He said: Can you feed sixty poor persons? He said: No. He said: Sit down. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a basket containing dates, and the basket is a large hamper, and he said: Take this and give it in charity. He said: Upon one poorer than us? There is no household between its two lava plains poorer than us. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his molar teeth appeared. He said: Take this and feed your family with it. Abu Muhammad said: And al-Layth ibn Sad, and Mamar, and Ismail ibn Umayyah, and al-Awzai, and Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah, and Uqayl, and Irak ibn Malik, and Ibn Abi Hafsah, and Mansur ibn al-Mutamir narrated from al-Zuhri: I had intercourse with my wife; can you free a slave? or to this effect."
"401","Malik, Ibn Jurayj, and Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari said: that a man broke fast in Ramadan, so he ordered him to expiate by freeing a slave, or fasting, or feeding."
"402","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Musaddad narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is overcome by vomiting while fasting, there is no makeup upon him, but if he induces vomiting, let him make up."
"403","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma al-Rahabi, from Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him): that while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was walking in al-Baqi in Ramadan, there was a man being cupped, and he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken fast."
"404","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from Abu Rafi, he said: I entered upon Abu Musa while he was being cupped at night, and I said: Why was this not done in the daytime? He said: Are you ordering me to shed my blood while I am fasting, when I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The cupper and the one cupped have broken fast."
"405","Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Waki narrated to us, from Shubah, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped at al-Qahah while fasting. Abu Muhammad said: And he was on a journey."
"406","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus informed us, from Awf, from Khilas ibn Amr, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats forgetfully, or drinks forgetfully, let him complete his fast, for it is only Allah who fed him and gave him drink."
"407","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you fasts and eats or drinks forgetfully, let him complete his fast, for it is only Allah who fed him and gave him drink."
"408","Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her): that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss and embrace while fasting, and he was the most in control of his desire among you (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"409","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sumayy, that he heard Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, that he heard Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) saying: Dawn would overtake the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in a state of janabah, then he would bathe and fast."
"410","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Asim ibn Umar, from Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the night approaches and the day turns away and the sun has set, then you have broken fast."
"411","Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya, he is al-Qattan, narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting. It was said: But you fast continuously? He said: I am not like any of you; I spend the night fed and given drink."
"412","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah, or one of them, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the crescent, fast, and when you see it, break fast; and if it is obscured from you, then fast thirty days."
"413","Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ribi, from one of the Companions of the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The people woke up fasting, completing thirty days, then two Bedouins came and testified that they had sighted the crescent yesterday, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the people, and they broke fast."
"414","Abu Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: Hamzah al-Aslami asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fasting while traveling. He said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"415","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted in the year of the Conquest, until when he reached al-Kadid he broke fast, and only the last of the actions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is to be taken. Abu Muhammad said: His saying, and only the last is to be taken, is from the saying of al-Zuhri; Mamar clarified that. Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us."
"416","Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya, meaning Ibn Said, narrated to us, from Shubah, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Hasan, from Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and saw a man with a crowd around him, shaded over, and said: What is this? They said: A fasting man. He said: It is not righteousness, or righteousness is not, that you fast while traveling."
"417","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Nafi ibn Yazid informed us, he said: Ibn al-Had narrated to me that Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to him, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that she said: One of us would break fast in Ramadan and could not make it up until Shaban came; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not fast in any month as he fasted in Shaban; he would fast it all except a little, indeed he would fast it all."
"418","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Ubayd, he said: I attended Eid with Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), and he began with the prayer before the sermon, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting these two days. And Sufyan said another time: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting these two days: the day of Fitr and the day of Adha. As for the day of Fitr, it is your breaking fast from your fasting, and as for Adha, you eat from the meat of your sacrifices."
"419","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one night in the month of Ramadan in the mosque, with people along with him. Then he prayed the second night, and more people gathered that night than the first. When it was the third or fourth night, the mosque filled until it was crowded with its people, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not come out to them. The people began calling to him: The prayer! But he did not come out to them. When morning came, Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: The people kept waiting for you last night, O Messenger of Allah! He said: Their affair was not hidden from me, but I feared it would be made obligatory upon them."
"420","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jurashi, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr al-Hadrami, from Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We fasted Ramadan with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not lead us in prayer in any part of the month, until when seven days remained he led us until a third of the night had gone. Then he did not lead us on the sixth remaining night, and he led us on the night after it until nearly half the night had gone. We said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would lead us in extra prayer for the rest of this night of ours! He said: When a man stands with the imam until he leaves, the rest of his night is counted for him. Then he did not lead us on the sixth night, and he led us on the seventh, and he sent for his family and the people gathered, and he led us until we feared we would miss al-falah. I said: What is al-falah? He said: Sahur."
"421","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Ibn al-Muqri said: and he said once: raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven, and whoever stands Laylat al-Qadr with faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven."
"422","Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek it in the last ten, in its odd nights, meaning Laylat al-Qadr."
"423","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, informed us, he said: Jabir ibn Yazid ibn Rifah narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Sulayman, he said: I heard Zirr ibn Hubaysh saying: Were it not for your fools, I would place my hands in my ears, then call out: Indeed Laylat al-Qadr is in Ramadan, in the last ten, in the last seven, three before it and three after it, the report of one who did not lie to me, from the report of one who did not lie to him, meaning Ubayy ibn Kab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"424","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar and Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued to observe itikaf in the last ten of Ramadan until Allah Almighty took him."
"425","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yala ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Amrah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to observe itikaf, he would pray Fajr, then enter the place where he wanted to observe itikaf. He wanted to observe itikaf in the last ten of Ramadan, so he ordered and a tent was pitched for him, and Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) ordered and a tent was pitched for her, and Hafsah ordered and a tent was pitched for her. When Zaynab saw their two tents, she ordered and a tent was pitched for her. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, he said: Is it righteousness you intend? So he did not observe itikaf in Ramadan, and observed itikaf for ten days in Shawwal."
"426","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah and Amrah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: When I would come to the house in which there was a sick person, I would only ask about him while passing by, while she was in itikaf. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would put his head into my room while he was in the mosque, and I would comb it while he was in itikaf, and he would not enter the house for any need except when he needed ablution, while in itikaf."
"427","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, is Hajj every year? He said: No, rather one Hajj; then whoever wishes may voluntarily do more after that. Had I said every year, it would have been every year."
"428","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): that a woman lifted a boy of hers from a litter and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there Hajj for this one? He said: Yes, and you have reward."
"429","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Dhu al-Hulayfah for the people of Madinah, al-Juhfah for the people of Sham, and Qarn for the people of Najd, and it was mentioned to me, though I did not hear, that he appointed Yalamlam for the people of Yemen."
"430","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both). And Ibn Tawus, from his father, both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Dhu al-Hulayfah for the people of Madinah, al-Juhfah for the people of Sham, and Qarn for the people of Najd, and Ibn Tawus said: Qarn al-Manazil, and for the people of Yemen, Yalamlam, Amr said: and Ibn Tawus said: Alamlam. He said: They are for their people and for whoever passes them from other than their people, and whoever is nearer than them, Amr said: then from his family, and Ibn Tawus said: then from wherever he begins, likewise, so likewise, even the people of Makkah enter ihram from it."
"431","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his ihram before he entered ihram, and for his release before he circumambulated the House."
"432","Muhammad ibn Said al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Ubaydah informed us, he said: Mansur informed us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: It is as if I am looking at the glistening of perfume in the parting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram."
"433","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both): that a man called out and said: O Messenger of Allah, what should a muhrim avoid of clothing? He said: He should not wear trousers, nor a shirt, nor a hooded cloak, nor a turban, nor any garment touched by saffron or wars, and let one of you enter ihram in a waist-wrapper, a cloak, and sandals; if he does not find sandals, let him wear leather socks and cut them until they are below the ankles."
"434","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Amr, from Jabir, meaning Ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering a sermon, saying: Trousers are for one who does not find a waist-wrapper, and leather socks are for one who does not find sandals. And I do not know which of the two hadiths abrogated the other."
"435","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid, from Mujahid, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while in ihram, and when riders passed by us we would let down the garment from behind us over our faces, and it would not come from here, meaning from the side of her cheeks; when they passed, we would remove it. And she said: A muhrim woman may wear whatever she wishes except the face-veil."
"436","Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Abbad, meaning Ibn al-Awwam, narrated to us, from Hilal, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that Dubaah bint al-Zubayr came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to perform Hajj; shall I stipulate? He said: Yes. She said: What should I say? He said: Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, my release from the land is wherever You detain me."
"437","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Dubaah bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and she said: I want to perform Hajj but I am ill? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform Hajj and stipulate that my release is wherever You detain me. Al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya said: The hadith of Abd al-Razzaq in our view is preserved regarding the story of Dubaah (may Allah be pleased with her), cited as proof for one who wants to stipulate in Hajj."
"438","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for Hajj, and some people entered ihram with him for it, and some people entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah, and I was among those who entered ihram for Umrah."
"439","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the Farewell Hajj, and we entered ihram for Umrah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a sacrificial animal with him, let him enter ihram for Hajj along with Umrah, then let him not exit ihram until he exits from both together."
"440","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah."
"441","And Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these two hands of mine, yet he would not avoid anything that a muhrim avoids. And Abd al-Rahman said: Nor would he withdraw from anything, nor leave it. She said: And we do not know anything that releases a pilgrim except circumambulation of the House."
"442","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan al-Araj, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Dhuhr at Dhu al-Hulayfah, then his she-camel was brought and he marked it on the right side of its hump, then wiped the blood from it, then garlanded it with two sandals. Then his mount was brought and he rode it, and when it stood upright with him at al-Bayda, he entered ihram."
"443","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Musa ibn Salamah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent eighteen sacrificial camels with a man, and gave him instruction concerning them. He set out, then returned to him and said: What if one of them becomes exhausted under my care? He said: Slaughter it, then dye its sandals in its blood, then place them on its side, and neither you nor anyone of your traveling party may eat from it."
"444","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent garlanded sheep as sacrificial animals."
"445","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Uthman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man with a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a sacrificial camel. He said: Woe to you, or fie on you, ride it."
"446","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you, in the second or third time."
"447","Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya, meaning Ibn Said, narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata narrated to me, he said: I heard Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) being asked about riding sacrificial camels? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Ride it properly when you are compelled to it, until you find another mount."
"448","Muhammad ibn Wazir al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying the talbiyah: Labbayk, for Umrah and Hajj together."
"449","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah, he said: I mentioned to Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for Umrah and Hajj. He said: May Allah have mercy on Anas, he is mistaken; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only entered ihram for Hajj, and we entered ihram with him for it."
"450","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qays, meaning Ibn Muslim, from Tariq, from Abu Musa, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was dismounted at al-Batha. He said to me: Have you performed Hajj? I said: Yes. He said: How did you do it? He said: I said: Labbayk, with an ihram like the ihram of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: You have done well; go and circumambulate the House and al-Safa and al-Marwah, then exit ihram. He said: So I circumambulated the House and al-Safa and al-Marwah."
"451","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Ismail, meaning Ibn Ulayyah, informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both): that the talbiyah of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayk, there is no partner for You, labbayk; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; there is no partner for You. He said: And Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) added: Labbayk, and glad tidings to You, and good is in Your hands, and longing and deed are to You."
"452","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, that he heard Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informing, from Khallad ibn al-Saib, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), raising it, Ibn al-Muqri said, and he said once: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said once: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril came to me and ordered me to command my Companions to raise their voices with the ihram call, or with the talbiyah."
"453","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah narrating from his father that he was with some people among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while they were in ihram, and Abu Qatadah was not in ihram. He rode a horse and struck down a wild donkey, and ate from its meat, but his companions refused to eat. They asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Did you point, or kill, or hunt it? They said: No. He said: There is no harm in it; eat it."
"454","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Saab (may Allah be pleased with him). And Ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Malik ibn Anas, Ibn Abi Dhib, and al-Layth informed me that Ibn Shihab informed them, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): that al-Saab ibn Jaththamah (may Allah be pleased with him) gifted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a wild donkey while he was at al-Abwa or Waddan, and he returned it to him. He said: When he saw what was in my face, he said: We only returned it to you because we are in ihram. And Ibn Uyaynah said in this: The meat of a donkey. And Said ibn Jubayr said, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): The rump of a donkey."
"455","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, that Ibn Wahb informed them, from Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn Salim and Yaqub ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri, that Amr, the freedman of al-Muttalib, informed them both, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The meat of land game is lawful for you while you are in ihram, as long as you did not hunt it, nor was it hunted for you."
"456","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd, from Ibn Abi Ammar, he said: I asked Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) about the hyena? He said: Eat it. He said: I said: Shall I eat it? He said: Yes, eat it by my order. I said: Is it game? He said: Yes. I said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes."
"457","Ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim informed me, from Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ammar narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he was asked about the hyena. He said: It is game, and in it is a ram."
"458","Ibn al-Muqri and Ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five animals, there is no sin in killing them for whoever kills them in the Sanctuary and in ihram, and Ibn Hashim said: in the lawful land and the Sanctuary: the mouse, the kite, the crow, the scorpion, and the vicious dog."
"459","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from his father: Ibn Abbas and al-Miswar ibn Makhramah (may Allah be pleased with them both) disputed about a muhrim washing his head while they were at al-Arj, so they sent me to Abu Ayyub. I came to him and found him bathing between the two posts of a well. I greeted him, and he drew his garment to his chest. I said: The son of your brother sent me to you, asking you how you saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washing his head? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washing his head like this, bringing his two hands forward and back over his head. He said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washing his head."
"460","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, and Ata and Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram."
"461","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, meaning Ibn Musa, from Nubayh, he said: Umar ibn Ubaydullah ibn Mamar complained of his eyes, and when he came to al-Rawha it intensified. He sent to Aban ibn Uthman, and Aban sent word that Uthman narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Bandage them both with aloes."
"462","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar al-Zahrani informed us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Nubayh ibn Wahb, from Aban ibn Uthman, from Uthman ibn Affan (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A muhrim should not marry, nor give in marriage, nor propose."
"463","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, the son of the sister of Maymunah bint al-Harith, from Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me at Sarif while we were both in a state of lawful release."
"464","Ibn al-Muqri and Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, and the hadith is that of Ibn al-Muqri, from Amr, from Abu al-Shatha, that Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) while in ihram. I informed al-Zuhri of it, and he said: Yazid ibn al-Asamm, and she is his maternal aunt, informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her while in lawful release, and she was in lawful release."
"465","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata informed me that Safwan ibn Yala ibn Umayyah informed him that Yala used to say to Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him): Would that I could see the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when revelation descends upon him. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at al-Jiranah, wearing a garment shaded over him, with some of his Companions with him, among them Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), a man came to him wearing a jubbah, smeared with perfume, and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who entered ihram for Umrah after smearing himself with perfume? The Prophet looked at him for a while, then fell silent, and revelation came to him. Umar gestured with his hand to Yala ibn Umayyah: Come. He said: Yala came and put his head in, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was red-faced, snoring for a while, then it was lifted from him. He said: Where is the questioner who asked me about Umrah just now? The man was sought and brought. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for the perfume on you, wash it three times, and as for the jubbah, remove it, then do in your Umrah as you do in your Hajj."
"466","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: And Ata used to hold to the ruling of the man with the jubbah before the Farewell Hajj, and the later, the later of the commands of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is more deserving. And of the affair of the man with the jubbah, Ata informed me that Safwan ibn Yala ibn Umayyah informed him that Yala used to say the like of it."
"467","Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Safwan ibn Yala, from his father, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Jiranah, and a man came to him wearing a cut-out garment, meaning a jubbah, smeared with khaluq perfume, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have entered ihram for Umrah while wearing this? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What would you do in your Hajj? He said: I would remove this cut-out garment and wash off this khaluq. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever you would do in your Hajj, do it in your Umrah."
"468","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Malik ibn Anas informed me, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Kab ibn Ujrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that he was with the Messenger of Allah in ihram, and lice troubled him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to shave his head and said: Fast three days, or feed six poor persons, two mudds each, or sacrifice a sheep; whichever of these you do suffices for you."
"469","Muhammad ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stop the talbiyah in Umrah when he touched the Stone."
"470","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Asbagh narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb informed me, he said: Yunus and Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, that his father narrated to him, he said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) kissed the Stone, then said: By Allah, I know you are a stone; were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing you, I would not kiss you."
"471","Amr said: And Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me the like of it, from his father."
"472","Abu Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah informed me, from Nafi, he said: I saw Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) touch the Stone with his hand, then kiss his hand, and say: I have not left it since I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing it."
"473","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Adam informed me, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Makkah, he came to the Stone and touched it, then moved to his right, trotting three circuits and walking four."
"474","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb informed us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trotted from the Stone to the Stone three times, and walked four times."
"475","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Ubayd, the freedman of al-Saib, informed me that his father informed him that Abdullah ibn al-Saib informed him that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying between the corner of Banu Jumah and the Black Corner: Our Lord, give us good in this world, and good in the Hereafter, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire."
"476","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad, he said: Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Circumambulation of the House, and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and stoning the pillars were only instituted for establishing the remembrance of Allah Almighty."
"477","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Men of knowledge informed me, among them Malik ibn Anas, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she said: As for those who combined Hajj and Umrah, they only performed one circumambulation."
"478","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed one circumambulation for their Hajj and Umrah, and ran between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Abu Asim said once: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions circumambulated the House with one circumambulation for their Hajj and Umrah, and ran between al-Safa and al-Marwah."
"479","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Mansur narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters ihram for Hajj and Umrah, one circumambulation suffices him for both, then let him not exit ihram until he exits from both."
"480","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Musa narrated to us. He said: And Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Circumambulation of the House is prayer, but Allah has permitted speech in it for you; so whoever speaks, let him speak only good."
"481","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwa, from Zaynab bint Umm Salama, from Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her): that she arrived while she was ill and mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Perform tawaf behind the people while you are riding."
"482","She said: And I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at the Ka'ba reciting Surah al-Tur."
"483","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed tawaf during the Farewell Hajj upon a camel, touching the Corner with a mihjan (a curved cane)."
"484","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Harawi - who resided in al-Rayy - narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ma'ruf, from Abu al-Tufayl (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing tawaf upon his mount, touching the Corner with his mihjan and kissing the tip of the mihjan, then he went out to al-Safa and performed seven circuits upon his mount."
"485","Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ja'far narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: We came to Jabir ibn Abd Allah while he was among Banu Salima and we asked him about the Hajj of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Madina for nine years without performing Hajj, then it was announced among the people that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform Hajj this year, so many people descended upon Madina, all of them seeking to follow the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and to do as he did. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out when five days remained of Dhu al-Qa'da, and we set out with him, until when he came to Dhu al-Hulayfa, Asma bint Umays gave birth to Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, so she sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him: What should I do? He said: Perform ghusl, then wrap yourself with a cloth, then enter ihram. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out until when his she-camel rose with him upon al-Bayda, he declared tawhid with the talbiya: Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayk la sharika laka labbayk, inna al-hamda wa al-ni'mata laka wa al-mulk, la sharika lak. And the people recited the talbiya, and the people added: Dha al-Ma'arij and the like. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard but said nothing to them. I looked as far as my eyesight extended in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): riders and walkers, and behind him likewise, and to his right likewise, and to his left likewise. Jabir said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us, the Qur'an was being revealed upon him and he knew its interpretation, so whatever he acted upon of it, we acted upon. We set out intending nothing but Hajj, until when we came to the Ka'ba, the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touched the Black Stone, then walked briskly (ramal) for three circuits and walked normally for four, until when he finished he went to the Maqam of Ibrahim (peace be upon him) and prayed two rak'as behind it, then he recited: And take the Maqam of Ibrahim as a place of prayer. My father said: And he recited therein Surah al-Tawhid and: Say, O you disbelievers. Then he touched the Stone and went out to al-Safa, then he recited: Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwa are among the symbols of Allah. Then he said: We begin with what Allah began with. So he ascended al-Safa until when he looked at the House he proclaimed takbir, then said: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Competent; there is no god but Allah, He fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the Confederates alone. Then he supplicated, then he returned to these words, then he descended until when his feet poured forth in the valley he walked briskly, until when he ascended he walked, until when he came to al-Marwa he ascended it, until when he looked at the House, he said upon it as he had said upon al-Safa. When it was the seventh at al-Marwa, he said: O people, had I known beforehand what I know now, I would not have brought the sacrificial animals and I would have made it an Umra, so whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him exit ihram and make it an Umra. He said: So all the people exited ihram, and Suraqa ibn Ju'shum said while he was at the bottom of al-Marwa: O Messenger of Allah, is this for our year only or forever? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) interlaced his fingers and said: Forever - three times - then he said: Umra has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection. He said: And Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) arrived from Yemen, bringing sacrificial animals, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had brought sacrificial animals with him from Madina, and Fatima (may Allah be pleased with her) had exited ihram and worn dyed garments and applied kohl, so Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) disapproved of that in her, so she said: My father commanded me with it. Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said in Kufa - my father said: This phrase Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) did not mention - so I went, inciting, to seek a verdict from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about what Fatima had mentioned. I said: Fatima wore dyed garments and applied kohl, and said: My father commanded me with it. He said: She spoke the truth, she spoke the truth, I commanded her with it. Jabir said: And he said to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): With what did you enter ihram? He said: I said: O Allah, I enter ihram with what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enters ihram with. He said: And I have the sacrificial animals with me, he said: Then do not exit ihram. He said: And the total of the sacrificial animals which Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) brought from Yemen and which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought was one hundred. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered sixty-three with his own hand and gave to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who slaughtered the rest, and he made him a partner in his sacrifice. Then he ordered a piece from each camel to be placed in a pot, and they ate from its meat and drank from its broth. Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have slaughtered here, and Mina in its entirety is a place of slaughter. And he stood at Arafat and said: I have stood here, and Arafat in its entirety is a standing place. And he stood at al-Muzdalifa and said: I have stood here, and al-Muzdalifa in its entirety is a standing place."
"486","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: We set out intending nothing but Hajj, but when we were at Sarif I menstruated, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while I was weeping, and he said: Have you menstruated? I said: Yes. He said: This is something Allah has decreed for the daughters of Adam, so perform what the pilgrim in ihram performs, except that you do not perform tawaf of the House."
"487","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Zakariyya, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwa ibn Mudaress (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at al-Muzdalifa, and I said: I have come to you from the two mountains of Tayy, and I have exhausted my mount and I left no mountain but I stood upon it. He said: Whoever witnesses the prayer with us and stands at Arafat by night or day, has fulfilled his tafath (completed the rites removing ihram restrictions) and his Hajj is complete."
"488","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Thawri narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Ata, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'mar al-Dili, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Hajj is Arafat - three times - so whoever reaches Arafat before dawn breaks has indeed attained Hajj."
"489","Jamil ibn al-Hasan wrote to me, he said: Mahbub - meaning Ibn al-Hasan - narrated to us, he said: Dawud narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at Arafat, and when he said: Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, he said: The only true good is the good of the Hereafter."
"490","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'a, he said: Zayd ibn Ali narrated to us, from his father, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the standing place at Arafat and stood, and said: This is the standing place, and all of Arafat is a standing place, then he moved on (afada) when the sun had set."
"491","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I was among those whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ahead from al-Muzdalifa among the weak of his family."
"492","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Awf, from Ziyad ibn al-Husayn, from Abu al-Aliya, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me on the morning of al-Aqaba while he was upon his mount: Bring me pebbles. So I picked for him pebbles like those used for khadhf (small tossing), and when I placed them in his hand he said: Like these - three times - and beware of extremism in religion, for those before you were destroyed only by extremism in religion."
"493","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them both) saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stone on the Day of Sacrifice in the forenoon, and as for after that, then after the sun had declined."
"494","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shu'ba, from al-Hakam and Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: Abd Allah stoned the Jamra with seven pebbles, placing the House to his left and Arafat to his right, and said: This is the standing place of the one upon whom Surah al-Baqara was revealed."
"495","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata informed me, he said: Ibn Abbas informed me that al-Fadl informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued reciting the talbiya until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqaba."
"496","Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Bakr who heard his father narrating from Abu al-Baddah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave concession to the shepherds to stone one day and leave one day."
"497","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, from his father, from Abu al-Baddah ibn Asim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave concession to the camel-herds regarding staying overnight: that they stone on the Day of Sacrifice, then combine the stoning of the two days after the Sacrifice and throw them on one of them. Malik said: I thought he said: On the first of them; then they stone on the day of departure (yawm al-nafr)."
"498","Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr that he heard Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: We shared with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Hajj and Umra, every seven in one camel."
"499","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, he said: Amra bint Abd al-Rahman al-Ansariyya informed me, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she heard her saying: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and on the Day of Sacrifice beef was brought to us, so I said: What is this? It was said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered on behalf of his wives. Yahya said: So I mentioned it to al-Qasim, and he said: By Allah, she conveyed the hadith to you correctly."
"500","Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'ba, he said: And Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Ubayd ibn Fayruz, he said: I asked al-Bara, saying: Narrate to me what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade, or what he disliked, of sacrificial animals? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us - and my hand is shorter than his hand - and said: Four are not permissible: the one-eyed whose blindness is evident, the sick whose sickness is evident, the lame whose lameness is evident, and the broken-boned whose marrow is gone. He said: I said: I dislike that there be a defect in the teeth, or in the ear, or in the horn. He said: What you dislike, leave it, but do not forbid it to anyone."
"501","Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: al-Hasan ibn Muslim and Abd al-Karim al-Jazari informed me that Mujahid informed them, that Ibn Abi Layla informed him, that Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to take charge of his sacrificial camels, and to distribute their meat and hides, and not to give anything of them for the butchering work."
"502","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to take charge of his sacrificial camels, and to distribute their meat and coverings, and he commanded me not to give the butcher anything of them. And he said: We give him from our own."
"503","Sulayman ibn Shu'ayb al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shaved his head, he began with the right side of his head and gave it to Abu Talha, then he shaved the left side of his head and distributed it among the people."
"504","Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Ijli narrated to us, he said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy upon those who shave. They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: May Allah have mercy upon those who shave. They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: May Allah have mercy upon those who shave. They said: And those who shorten? He said: And those who shorten."
"505","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ifada (went from Mina to Mecca for the tawaf) on the Day of Sacrifice, then returned and prayed Dhuhr at Mina. Nafi' said: Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to perform ifada on the Day of Sacrifice, then return and pray Dhuhr at Mina, and he mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did it."
"506","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Isa ibn Talha, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked by a man who said: I slaughtered before shaving? He said: Shave, and there is no harm. Another asked him, saying: I shaved before slaughtering? He said: Slaughter, and there is no harm. Another said: I slaughtered before stoning? He said: Stone, and there is no harm."
"507","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Isa ibn Talha, from Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon his she-camel at Mina, and a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I thought shaving came before sacrifice, so I shaved before sacrificing? He said: Sacrifice, and there is no harm. And another came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I thought shaving came before stoning, so I shaved before stoning? He said: Stone, and there is no harm. He said: He was not asked that day about anything a man had done out of order except that he said: Do it, and there is no harm."
"508","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ibn Shihab saying: Isa ibn Talha narrated to me, he said: Abd Allah ibn Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated to me: that while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon on the Day of Sacrifice, a man stood up to him and said: I did not think... and he mentioned the hadith. Abu Muhammad said: And in it is from Abu Bakra and Nubayt ibn Sharit and Ibn Umar."
"509","Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Abu Usama narrated to us. And al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Uqba narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Nafi' narrated to me, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both): that al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to spend the nights of Mina at Mecca on account of his duty of providing water (siqaya), so he permitted him. The wording of the hadith is that of al-Ashajj."
"510","Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, Nafi' informed me, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina two rak'as, and with Abu Bakr two rak'as, and with Umar two rak'as, and with Uthman two rak'as at the beginning of his rule, then Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) completed it (prayed four)."
"511","Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ifada at the end of his day when he had prayed Dhuhr, then returned and stayed at Mina the nights of the days of Tashriq, stoning each Jamra when the sun had declined, each Jamra with seven pebbles, proclaiming takbir with each pebble, and standing at the first and the second, prolonging the standing and supplicating fervently, then stoning the third and not standing at it."
"512","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Qatada ibn Di'ama informed him, from Anas ibn Malik who narrated to him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Dhuhr and Asr and Maghrib and Isha, and slept a sleep at al-Muhassab, then rode to the House and performed tawaf of it."
"513","Muhammad ibn Wazir al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Ishaq al-Azraq, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', he said: I said to Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): Narrate to me something you comprehended from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Where did he pray Dhuhr on the day of Tarwiya? He said: At Mina. I said: And where Asr on the day of departure (yawm al-nafr)? He said: At al-Abtah. Then he said: Do as your rulers do."
"514","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sulayman - he is al-Ahwal - from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The people were departing in every direction, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no one depart until his last covenant is with the House (i.e., performs the farewell tawaf)."
"515","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: Safiyya bint Huyayy menstruated after having performed ifada, and that was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Is she going to detain us? I said: She menstruated after having performed ifada. He said: Then no (she may leave)."
"516","Ibn al-Muqri and Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, and Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Ibn Uyayna informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): that a woman from Khath'am asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - Ibn Khashram and Ibn Hashim added: On the morning of the Sacrifice - they said: And al-Fadl was his riding companion behind him - she said: The obligation of Allah in Hajj upon His servants has come upon my father while he is an old man who cannot hold himself steady upon the mount, so do you see that Hajj may be performed on his behalf? He said: Yes."
"517","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa informed us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Musa ibn Salama, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a certain al-Juhani asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: My father is a very old man who died without performing Hajj - or he said: cannot perform Hajj? He said: Then perform Hajj on his behalf."
"518","Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Azra, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: Labbayk on behalf of Shubruma. He said: Who is Shubruma? He said: A brother of mine, or a relative of mine. He said: Have you ever performed Hajj? He said: No. He said: Then make this on your own behalf, then recite talbiya on behalf of Shubruma."
"519","Amr ibn Abd Allah al-Awdi and Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Waki' narrated to us, from Shu'ba, from al-Nu'man ibn Salim - Ibn Hashim added: and he was trustworthy - from Amr ibn Aws, from Abu Razin al-Uqayli (may Allah be pleased with him), that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father is a very old man who cannot perform Hajj and Umra nor travel? He said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your father and Umra."
"520","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Shu'ba, from Ja'far ibn Iyas, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My sister vowed to perform Hajj and she died? He said: Had she owed a debt, would you have paid it? He said: Yes. He said: Then pay Allah, for He is most deserving of fulfillment."
"521","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The accepted Hajj has no reward but Paradise, and Umra to Umra expiates what is between them."
"522","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us - with the like of it."
"523","Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata informed me, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a woman of the Ansar - Ibn Abbas named her but I forgot her name: What prevented you from performing Hajj with us this year? She said: O Prophet of Allah, I had two water-carrying camels; Abu so-and-so and his son - meaning her husband and her son - rode one, and left one camel upon which water is drawn. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Ramadan comes, perform Umra, for an Umra in it equals a Hajj, or he said: equals a Hajj."
"524","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us from what he narrated to us of the military expeditions (maghazi), he said: Ma'mar said: al-Zuhri said: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from al-Miswar ibn Makhrama and Marwan ibn al-Hakam, each one of them confirming the hadith of his companion, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out at the time of al-Hudaybiya among some ten-odd hundred of his Companions, until when they were at Dhu al-Hulayfa, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) garlanded the sacrificial animals and entered ihram for Umra, and sent ahead of him a scout of his from Khuza'a to inform him about Quraysh, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marched until when he was at Ghadir al-Ashtat near Usfan, his Khuza'i scout came to him and said: I left Ka'b ibn Lu'ayy and Amir ibn Lu'ayy having gathered against you the Ahabish, and gathered against you throngs, and they will fight you and bar you from the House. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Advise me - Ibn Yahya mentioned the hadith at length concerning the polytheists barring them from the House - and he said at its end after mentioning the case: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Stand, slaughter, then shave. And he mentioned the rest of the hadith."
"525","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Amr who heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr informing that he heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man fell from his camel and his neck was broken, and he died while in ihram. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and sidr (lote leaves), and shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his head, for Allah will resurrect him on the Day of Resurrection reciting talbiya."
"526","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Abida - meaning Ibn Humayd - narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir narrated to me, from al-Hakam ibn Utayba, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A she-camel broke the neck of a man while he was in ihram and he died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that he be shrouded in his two garments and washed, and his face not be covered, nor perfume touched, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection reciting talbiya."
"527","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid ibn Mazyad informed us that his father informed him, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, he said: Abu Salama narrated to me, he said: Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me, he said: When Mecca was conquered, Hudhayl killed a man from Banu Layth for a killing of theirs in pre-Islamic times. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he stood and said: Indeed Allah withheld the Elephant from Mecca and gave His Messenger and the believers dominion over it, and it was not lawful for anyone before me, nor is it lawful for anyone after me, and it was made lawful for me only for an hour of a day, and it at this hour of mine is sacred: its trees are not to be cut, nor its thorns uprooted, nor its lost property picked up except by one who announces it, and whoever has one killed, he has the better of two choices: either he is given retaliation (qisas) or he takes blood-money. So a man from the people of Yemen called Abu Shah stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, write for me! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Write for Abu Shah. Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, except idhkhir (aromatic grass), for we use it in our houses and graves. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Except idhkhir, except idhkhir."
"528","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Abida ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Mecca: Indeed this land is sacred; Allah made it sacred the day He created the heavens and the earth, so it is sacred by the sanctity of Allah until the Day of Resurrection. Killing in it was not made lawful for anyone except me, nor is it lawful for anyone after me until the Hour comes. Its thorns are not to be cut, nor its vegetation uprooted, nor its game frightened away."
"529","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Were I to see gazelles in Madina I would not frighten them; indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between its two lava plains is sacred. Malik said: The sanctuary of Madina is a barid by a barid, and the two labas are of trees, and they are the two harras (lava fields)."
"530","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sanctified what is between the two lava plains of Madina: its trees are not to be cut, nor its game frightened away."
"531","Ibn al-Muqri and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him) conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and Mahmud said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mounts are not saddled except to three mosques: al-Masjid al-Haram, al-Masjid al-Aqsa, and this mosque of mine."
"532","Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Kaysan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Instruct your dying ones: La ilaha illa Allah."
"533","Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr - meaning Ibn Shumayl - narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Hafsa, from Umm Atiyya (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: Among what was taken from us in the pledge was: that we not wail."
"534","Muhammad ibn Yahya and Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us, they said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two traits of pre-Islamic ignorance: impugning lineage, and wailing. Ibn Yahya said: And he said once: The people will never leave them."
"535","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman informed us. And Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Zubayd, from Ibrahim, from Masruq, from Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: He is not of us who strikes the cheeks, tears the garments, and calls with the call of pre-Islamic ignorance. And in the hadith of Ibn Hashim, he said: Zubayd narrated to me."
"536","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Yahya ibn Abbad narrated to me, from his father Abbad, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: When they intended to wash the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they differed concerning him, saying: By Allah, we do not know whether to strip the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of his garments as we strip our dead, or wash him with his garments upon him. She said: When they differed, Allah cast sleep upon them until there was not a man among them but his chin was upon his chest, then a speaker spoke to them from the direction of the house whom they did not know: Wash the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his shirt upon him. She said: So they stood to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), washing him with his shirt upon him, pouring water over the shirt and rubbing him with the shirt without their hands. He said: And Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) used to say: Had I known beforehand what I know now, none would have washed him but his wives. When they finished washing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he was shrouded in three garments: two Sahari garments and a Hibara cloak, wrapped therein layer upon layer."
"537","As Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Ali ibn al-Husayn; and al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them)."
"538","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Umm Atiyya (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us while we were washing his daughter, and said: Wash her three times, or five, or more than that if you see fit, with water and sidr, and place in the last camphor, or something of camphor, and when you finish, inform me. When we finished we informed him, so he threw to us his waist-wrap and said: Wrap her in it as the innermost garment."
"539","Al-Hasan ibn Arafa narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us from among the people, from Hafsa and Ibn Sirin, from Umm Atiyya (may Allah be pleased with her), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: And begin with her right sides and the places of ablution."
"540","Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Ya'la narrated to us, from Hisham, he said: Hafsa narrated to me, from Umm Atiyya (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: We braided the head of the daughter of the Messenger of Allah into three plaits and threw them behind her."
"541","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isa informed us, from Hisham, from his father, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three white Yemeni garments, in which there was neither shirt nor turban."
"542","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiya al-Darir narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Khabbab ibn al-Aratt (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the path of Allah seeking the Face of Allah, so our reward became due upon Allah. Among us are those who passed on without consuming anything of their reward, among them Mus'ab ibn Umayr, who was killed on the day of Uhud and nothing was found to shroud him in but a namira (a striped cloak): when we placed it upon his head his feet showed, and when we placed it upon his feet his head showed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Place it toward his head, and place idhkhir upon his feet. And among us are those whose fruits ripened for them and they are harvesting them."
"543","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isma'il informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Samura ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you are these white garments: let your living wear them, and shroud your dead in them."
"544","Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr who heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them both) saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the grave of Abd Allah ibn Ubayy after he had been placed in his pit, so he ordered that he be brought out, placed him upon his knees or thighs, blew upon him of his saliva, and clothed him in his shirt. And Allah knows best."
"545","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five are due for the Muslim upon his brother: returning the greeting of peace, invoking mercy upon the sneezer (tashmit), visiting the sick, following the funeral, and accepting the invitation."
"546","Ibn al-Muqri and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever walks with it until it is buried has two qirats, one of them - or the smaller of them - like Uhud. And Ibn al-Muqri said: And whoever follows it until it is finished."
"547","Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Hasten with the funeral, for if it is good, it is good you advance it to, and if it is evil, it is evil you cast off your necks."
"548","Ibn al-Muqri and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from Amir ibn Rabi'a (may Allah be pleased with him) conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and Mahmud said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you see the funeral, stand for it, until it passes you by or is placed down."
"549","Umar ibn Shabba narrated to us, he said: Ghundar narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir saying: I heard Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam saying: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stand for a funeral, so we stood, and I saw him sit, so we sat."
"550","Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Isma'il informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Ibn Rabi'a (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you see a funeral, if you are not walking with it, then stand for it until it passes you by or is placed down. He said: Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) would sometimes go ahead of the funeral and sit, then when he saw it approaching he would stand until it was placed down. He said: And sometimes he would be screened by it."
"551","Al-Hasan ibn Arafa narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibn Sirin and Hisham, from Hafsa and Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Umm Atiyya (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: We were forbidden from following funerals, but it was not made binding upon us."
"552","Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'ba, he said: Amr ibn Murra narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Each had been five and four, so he commanded four."
"553","Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'ba, he said: Amr ibn Murra narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla: that Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) used to proclaim four takbirs over our funerals, and that he proclaimed five takbirs over a funeral, so they asked him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to proclaim them (i.e., five), or: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proclaimed them."
"554","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Ibrahim informed me, he said: I heard Talha ibn Abd Allah, he said: I prayed behind Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) over a funeral and he recited therein the Fatiha of the Book, so I took his hand and said: You recite it? He said: It is Sunna and right."
"555","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Talha ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf, he said: I prayed with Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) in this manner."
"556","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Talha al-Taymi, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reciting over a funeral the Fatiha of the Book and a surah, raising his voice in recitation, and saying: I raised my voice only to let you know that it is Sunna, while the imam conceals it (recites quietly)."
"557","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Talha ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf, the brother of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: I prayed behind Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) over a funeral and he recited the Fatiha of the Book and a surah, raising his voice until we heard, then when he finished I took his hand and asked him about that, and he said: Sunna and right."
"558","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, with this chain, similar, and he said: And a surah."
"559","Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiya narrated to me, from Habib ibn Ubayd, who heard Jubayr ibn Nufayr al-Hadrami saying: I heard Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja'i saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a funeral, and I memorized of his supplication while he was saying: O Allah, forgive him and have mercy upon him, grant him well-being and pardon him, honor his abode, widen his entrance, wash him with water and snow and hail, purify him of sins as You purified the white garment of filth, replace for him a home better than his home, a family better than his family, and a spouse better than his spouse, admit him to Paradise, and protect him from the punishment of the grave. Until I wished that I were that deceased."
"560","Bahr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiya narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, who narrated to him from his father, from Awf (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - with the like of this hadith as well."
"561","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: I heard Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf narrating to Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: The Sunna in prayer over the funeral is that you proclaim takbir, then recite Umm al-Qur'an (the Fatiha), then invoke blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then supplicate sincerely for the deceased, and you recite only in the first takbira, then he gives salutation to himself to his right."
"562","Abu Ja'far al-Darimi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya - meaning Ibn Abi Kathir - from Abu Ibrahim, from his father, that he witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying over a deceased, and he said: O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our present and our absent, our young and our old, our male and our female."
"563","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: al-Shaybani narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated to me - and he claimed he witnessed it - he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a grave that had been buried at night, and said: Who is this? They said: This is the grave of so-and-so, who died last night, and we disliked disturbing you at night lest something befall you or we burden you, so we buried him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and we lined up behind him, and he prayed over him."
"564","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: I heard Malik ibn Anas narrating from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced to the people the death of al-Najashi on the day he died, and went out with them to the place of prayer, lined them up, and proclaimed four takbirs over him."
"565","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Husayn - meaning al-Mu'allim - informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from Samura ibn Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the mother of so-and-so who died in childbirth, and he stood at her middle."
"566","Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Nafi' claiming that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) prayed over nine funerals together, placing the men toward the imam and the women toward the qibla, lining them in one row. The funeral of Umm Kulthum bint Ali ibn Abi Talib - the wife of Umar ibn al-Khattab - and a son of hers called Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them) were placed together, the imam that day being Sa'id ibn al-As, and among the people were Ibn Abbas, Abu Hurayra, Abu Sa'id, and Abu Qatada (may Allah be pleased with them). The boy was placed toward the imam. A man said: So I disapproved of that, and I looked at Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayra and Abu Sa'id and Abu Qatada (may Allah be pleased with them) and said: What is this? They said: It is the Sunna."
"567","Ibrahim ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj said: And Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrating that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once delivered a sermon and mentioned a man among his Companions who had died and been shrouded in an inadequate shroud, and buried at night, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man be buried at night until prayer has been performed over him, unless a person is compelled to that. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you shrouds his brother, let him make the shroud good."
"568","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, he said: Abu Badr Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Khaythama narrated to me, he said: Isma'il al-Suddi informed me, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Al-Abbas and Ali and al-Fadl entered the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man of the Ansar cut his lahd (niche grave), and he is the one who cuts the niche graves of the martyrs' graves."
"569","Amr ibn Abd Allah al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Hammam ibn Yahya, from Qatada, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you place your dead in their graves, say: In the name of Allah, and upon the Sunna of the Messenger of Allah."
"570","Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Uqba narrated to me, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Jamra, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) saying: I placed in the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a red velvet cloth."
"571","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Najiya ibn Ka'b, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: O Messenger of Allah, your uncle has died - or: my father has died. He said: Go and bury him (hiding him in the earth). I said: He died a polytheist. He said: Go and bury him. So I buried him, then I came to him. He said: Go and perform ghusl."
"572","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhadir ibn al-Muwarri' narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Sa'id al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Amra bint Abd al-Rahman informed me that she heard Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Breaking the bone of the believer dead is like breaking it alive."
"573","Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Layth, from his father, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik that Jabir ibn Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them both) informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to gather two men of the slain of Uhud in one garment, then say: Which of them had taken more of the Qur'an? When he was pointed to one of them, he advanced him in the lahd, and said: I am a witness over these on the Day of Resurrection. And he ordered their burial in their blood, and prayer was not performed over them, nor were they washed."
"574","Ibn al-Muqri and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Aswad who heard Nubayh al-Anazi saying: I heard Jabir ibn Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them both) saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the slain of Uhud, after they had been moved to Madina, to be returned to the places where they fell. The wording of the hadith is that of Mahmud. And Ibn al-Muqri said: From Nubayh, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"575","Ibn al-Muqri and Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No three children of a Muslim die and he enters the Fire, except to fulfill the oath (i.e., the verse: there is none of you but will pass over it)."
"576","Abu Hashim Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with them both) saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying - and by Allah, I shall not hear anyone after him saying: I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed the lawful is clear and indeed the unlawful is clear, and between them are dubious matters. He said: And perhaps he said: dubious. And I shall strike for you a parable concerning that: Indeed Allah has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is His prohibitions, and whoever grazes around the sanctuary is about to graze within it, and whoever mixes with doubtful matters is about to venture further. Ibn Awn said: I do not know whether this is what he heard from al-Nu'man, or he said it of his own opinion."
"577","607 - Ali ibn Abi Isa and Hisham ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Majid - that is Ibn Abi Rawwad - narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one will ever die until he has completed his provision, so do not consider provision slow in coming; fear Allah, O people, and seek it in a seemly manner, and take what is lawful and leave what is unlawful."
"578","608 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim and Jami', and Abd al-Malik, from Abu Wa'il Shaqiq, from Qays ibn Abi Gharazah, he said: We used to trade in al-Baqi', and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us while we were called brokers, and he said: O company of merchants, and he named us with a name better than our name, then he said: This selling is attended by oaths and lying, so mix it with charity."
"579","609 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man had a claim of a camel of a certain age upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he came demanding repayment, and he said: Give him, but they found for him only a camel older than his, and he said: Give him, and he said: You have repaid me in full, may Allah repay you in full. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are the best in repayment."
"580","610 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak ibn Harb, from Suwayd ibn Qays, he said: I and Makhramah al-Abdi brought cloth from Hajar, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and bargained with us for trousers, and with us was a weigher who weighed for a wage, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the weigher: Weigh and give extra."
"581","611 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: If one of you is transferred to a solvent person, let him follow the transfer, and the delay of the rich is injustice."
"582","612 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that anything be sold in the mosque or bought in it."
"583","613 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Khusayfah informed me, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you see someone selling or buying in the mosque, say: May Allah not profit your trade! And if you see someone announcing a lost item in it, say: May Allah not return it to you!"
"584","614 - Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: Ibn Uyaynah informed us. And Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and Ali said: he attributes it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not engage in najsh (false bidding), and let no resident sell on behalf of a Bedouin, and let no man sell over the sale of his brother, and let no man propose over the proposal of his brother, and let no woman ask for the divorce of her sister."
"585","615 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man selling food, and it was revealed to him: Put your hand beneath it. So he put his hand in and found it to be different, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He who deceives us is not of us."
"586","616 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys a musarrat or a muhaffalah (an animal whose milk has been retained to deceive) has the option; if he wishes to keep it he keeps it, and if he wishes to return it he returns it along with a sa' of dates, not samra' (wheat)."
"587","617 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys a musarrat has the option for three days; if he wishes to keep it he keeps it, and if he wishes to return it he returns it along with a sa' of dates, not samra'. Wahb said: meaning wheat."
"588","618 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: that Habban ibn Munqidh had been struck in his head with a ma'mumah wound, so his tongue became heavy and he was cheated in selling, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him the option for three (days) in whatever he bought, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Sell and say: No khilabah (no deceit). Then I heard him saying: La khidhabah, la khidhabah [mispronounced]. [FLAG: narrator mispronounces khilabah as khidhabah]"
"589","619 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him: that a man of the Ansar used to trade at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was weakness in his intellect, so his people came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, place an interdiction upon so-and-so, for he trades while there is weakness in his intellect. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and forbade him from selling, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, I cannot refrain from selling. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you will not give up selling, then say: Ha and ha (take and give), and no khilabah (no deceit)."
"590","620 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Sa'igh informed us that Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to him, he said: al-Akhdar ibn Ajlan al-Taymi narrated to us, that he heard a shaykh of Banu Hanifah called Abu Bakr narrating from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will buy this cloak and cup? A man said: O Prophet of Allah, I will take them for a dirham. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will add over a dirham? A man said: I will take them, O Prophet of Allah, for two. He said: They are yours."
"591","621 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Umar ibn Malik informed me, from Abdillah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Zayd ibn Aslam, he said: I heard a man called Shahr - he was a merchant - asking Abdillah ibn Umar about sale by auction, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that one of you sell over the sale of another until he leaves it, except spoils and inheritances."
"592","622 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting the caravans, and whoever meets a caravan and buys from it, the seller has the option when he reaches the market."
"593","623 - Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that goods be met before they enter the markets."
"594","624 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Let no resident sell on behalf of a Bedouin."
"595","625 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no resident sell on behalf of a Bedouin; leave people so that some of them may benefit from others."
"596","626 - Abu Umayyah al-Tarsusi Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Ubaydullah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to sell two slave boys who were brothers, so I sold them and separated them, and I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Catch up with them and take them back, and do not sell them except together."
"597","627 - Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Muslim, from Masruq, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: When the last verses of Surat al-Baqarah were revealed in which riba is mentioned, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and recited them to the people, then he forbade trade in wine."
"598","628 - Ibn al-Muqri and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, saying - and it had reached him that a man sold wine - and he said: May Allah destroy so-and-so! Did he not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah destroy the Jews; fats were forbidden to them, so they melted them and sold them. Mahmud added: and they consumed their prices. And Mahmud said: I heard Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, saying: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said."
"599","629 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has forbidden the sale of wine, idols, carrion, and pigs. Some of the Muslims said: What do you think about the fats of carrion, with which skins and ships are greased and people use for lamps? He said: It is unlawful. May Allah destroy the Jews, for when fats were forbidden to them they melted them and sold them and consumed their price."
"600","630 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sulaym - narrated to us, he said: Isma'il - meaning Ibn Umayyah - narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord said: There are three of whom I am the opponent on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever I oppose I defeat: a man who gave (a pledge) by Me and then betrayed, a man who sold a free man and consumed his price, and a man who hired a worker and took full work from him but did not pay him his wage."
